window.LANGUAGE_DATA={"pronoun":{"A":[{"id":"pronoun-A-01","title":"The rain cover","image":"assets/illustrations/rain-cover.webp","passage":"Maya pulled a cover over the tent. {It} kept the bedding dry.","question":"Who or what does “It” refer to?","options":["the waterproof cover","Maya","the bedding"],"answer":"the waterproof cover","hint":"Look for the thing that keeps rain away.","why":"The waterproof cover keeps the bedding dry, so “it” refers to the cover.","alt":"Maya, a brown-skinned girl with two braids, and Ben, a fair-skinned boy with curly red hair, pull a waterproof teal rain cover tightly over an orange tent. Secure pegs and taut ropes are visible. Bedding remains dry inside the tent. A light rain shower falls in the woodland clearing."},{"id":"pronoun-A-02","title":"The school project","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","passage":"Lina opened her notebook. {She} began to write.","question":"Who or what does “She” refer to?","options":["Lina","the notebook","the desk"],"answer":"Lina","hint":"Find the person doing the writing.","why":"“She” refers to Lina, the person who begins writing.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words."},{"id":"pronoun-A-03","title":"Reading the map","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers studied a map. {They} wanted to find the trail.","question":"Who or what does “They” refer to?","options":["the two hikers","the map","the trail"],"answer":"the two hikers","hint":"The pronoun means more than one person.","why":"“They” refers to the two hikers who study the route.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"pronoun-A-04","title":"A windy afternoon","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"The kite climbed into the sky. Jamal watched {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the kite","the field","the string"],"answer":"the kite","hint":"What is rising above the field?","why":"Jamal is watching the kite, so “it” refers to the kite.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"pronoun-A-05","title":"At the park","image":"assets/illustrations/park-picnic.webp","passage":"Two friends chose a picnic spot. The basket belonged to {them}.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["the two friends","the basket","the bags"],"answer":"the two friends","hint":"Find the people who own the basket.","why":"“Them” refers to the two friends, not to their belongings.","alt":"Two friends, a girl with light-brown skin and glasses and a boy with black hair, sit on a clearly spread yellow picnic blanket in a green park. A woven picnic basket sits between their bags. Lunch containers and apple slices are on the blanket. A level grassy patch beside a broad park path."},{"id":"pronoun-A-06","title":"Ready to sail","image":"assets/illustrations/sailing-ropes.webp","passage":"The instructor checked the boat. {He} looked at the ropes.","question":"Who or what does “He” refer to?","options":["the instructor","the boat","the ropes"],"answer":"the instructor","hint":"Which person can examine the ropes?","why":"“He” refers to the instructor who checks the equipment.","alt":"An adult male sailing instructor checks neatly coiled ropes on a small training sailboat beside a sheltered marina dock. Two children in properly fastened life jackets watch attentively. The boat has a prominent pale sail, a safe simple hull and tidy rigging. Calm harbour water and distant colourful boats."},{"id":"pronoun-A-07","title":"Garden helpers","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","passage":"Sofia held a small bucket. She put weeds into {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the bucket","Sofia","the vegetable bed"],"answer":"the bucket","hint":"Find the container used for the weeds.","why":"The bucket is the container, so the highlighted “it” refers to the bucket.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands."},{"id":"pronoun-A-08","title":"Mixing the batter","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"Mila picked up a spoon. {Her} apron stayed clean.","question":"Who or what does “Her” refer to?","options":["Mila","the spoon","the bowl"],"answer":"Mila","hint":"Whose apron protects their clothes?","why":"“Her” means that the apron belongs to Mila.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"pronoun-A-09","title":"Science partners","image":"assets/illustrations/science-tray.webp","passage":"Ruby and Min shared a science table. {Their} tray caught the drips.","question":"Who or what does “Their” refer to?","options":["Ruby and Min","the cup","the drips"],"answer":"Ruby and Min","hint":"Look for the two people sharing the tray.","why":"“Their” refers to Ruby and Min, who prepared the experiment together.","alt":"Ruby, a fair-skinned girl with auburn hair, and Min, an East Asian boy with glasses, share a classroom science table. Wearing safety goggles, they pour water between clear cups above a shallow tray. A few drops land in the tray, keeping the surrounding table dry. Friendly teacher in the background."},{"id":"pronoun-A-10","title":"A snowy day","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","passage":"The children put on warm gloves. {These} kept their fingers warm.","question":"Who or what does “These” refer to?","options":["the gloves","the children","the snow"],"answer":"the gloves","hint":"Which plural things cover fingers?","why":"“These” refers to the gloves that cover the children’s fingers.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park."},{"id":"pronoun-A-11","title":"A sandcastle","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"Mei filled two buckets with sand. She carried {them} to the castle.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["the two buckets","Mei and her friend","the castle walls"],"answer":"the two buckets","hint":"The pronoun refers to the things Mei carries.","why":"“Them” refers to the two buckets Mei lifts and carries.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."},{"id":"pronoun-A-12","title":"At the station","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"The family waited on the platform. {They} watched for the train.","question":"Who or what does “They” refer to?","options":["the family members","the platform","the track"],"answer":"the family members","hint":"Which group is waiting for the train?","why":"“They” refers to the family members waiting together.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"pronoun-A-13","title":"A thirsty dog","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","passage":"The dog waited beside its bowl. {It} wanted a drink.","question":"Who or what does “It” refer to?","options":["the dog","the bowl","the walk"],"answer":"the dog","hint":"What living thing can want a drink?","why":"“It” refers to the thirsty dog.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them."},{"id":"pronoun-A-14","title":"On the field","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","passage":"Coach Lee called the players. She gave {them} a new drill.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["the players","Coach Lee","the football"],"answer":"the players","hint":"Who receives the coach’s instructions?","why":"“Them” refers to the players listening to the coach.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline."},{"id":"pronoun-A-15","title":"A book to share","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"Sofia chose a book. {Its} cover had a bright picture.","question":"Who or what does “Its” refer to?","options":["the book","Sofia","the table"],"answer":"the book","hint":"Which thing has a cover?","why":"“Its” means that the cover belongs to the book.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"pronoun-A-16","title":"The treehouse plan","image":"assets/illustrations/measuring-board.webp","passage":"The builder held a long board. The children measured {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the board","the builder","the children"],"answer":"the board","hint":"Find the thing being measured.","why":"The children measure the board, so “it” refers to the board.","alt":"An adult builder steadies a sturdy long wooden board flat on a low workbench while two children carefully measure it with a tape measure. All wear safety glasses. A small partly built treehouse appears safely at ground level behind them. No power tools in use, no readable measurements."},{"id":"pronoun-A-17","title":"The hiking group","image":"assets/illustrations/night-camp.webp","passage":"“{We} will stay together,” said the hikers.","question":"Who or what does “We” refer to?","options":["the hikers","the trail markers","the trees"],"answer":"the hikers","hint":"Who is speaking inside the quotation marks?","why":"The hikers say “we” to mean themselves as a group.","alt":"A small supervised group of young hikers stays together beside their campsite at dusk. A girl uses a torch to illuminate the woodland path, and a boy points toward their glowing tent. The adult guide is close beside them. A gentle moon and stars above; warm, reassuring night scene."},{"id":"pronoun-A-18","title":"The skateboard","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Finn pointed to the skateboard. “It belongs to {me},” he said.","question":"Who or what does “me” refer to?","options":["Finn","his friend","the instructor"],"answer":"Finn","hint":"Read the words that tell you who is speaking.","why":"Finn is speaking, so “me” refers to Finn.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"pronoun-A-19","title":"Bridge builders","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"Lina and Andre made a bridge. {Their} model stood on the table.","question":"Who or what does “Their” refer to?","options":["Lina and Andre","the craft sticks","the table"],"answer":"Lina and Andre","hint":"Who made and owns the model?","why":"The model belongs to its builders, Lina and Andre.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"pronoun-A-20","title":"Bike practice","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"The rider wore a helmet. The strap fitted under {her} chin.","question":"Who or what does “her” refer to?","options":["the rider","the bicycle","the instructor"],"answer":"the rider","hint":"Find the person wearing the helmet.","why":"“Her” refers to the rider whose chin is under the helmet strap.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"pronoun-A-21","title":"Flying together","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"A girl and a boy flew a kite. The wind pulled {their} kite upward.","question":"Who or what does “their” refer to?","options":["the girl and the boy","the nearby trees","the clouds"],"answer":"the girl and the boy","hint":"Which people are sharing the kite?","why":"“Their” refers to the girl and the boy sharing the kite.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"pronoun-A-22","title":"Picnic blanket","image":"assets/illustrations/park-picnic.webp","passage":"The blanket lay on the grass. The children sat on {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the blanket","their lunch","the tree"],"answer":"the blanket","hint":"Which thing was spread out for sitting?","why":"“It” refers to the blanket spread over the grass.","alt":"Two friends, a girl with light-brown skin and glasses and a boy with black hair, sit on a clearly spread yellow picnic blanket in a green park. A woven picnic basket sits between their bags. Lunch containers and apple slices are on the blanket. A level grassy patch beside a broad park path."},{"id":"pronoun-A-23","title":"A safe start","image":"assets/illustrations/life-jacket-check.webp","passage":"The instructor checked the children’s life jackets. {She} tightened a strap.","question":"Who or what does “She” refer to?","options":["the sailing instructor","a child’s jacket","the boat"],"answer":"the sailing instructor","hint":"Who checks and tightens the strap?","why":"“She” refers to the sailing instructor carrying out the checks.","alt":"An adult female sailing instructor in a navy jacket gently tightens a loose life-jacket strap on a child before boarding a small boat. Show the fitted life jacket and closed buckle prominently. Another child waits wearing a properly fastened life jacket. Calm marina dock, safely away from the edge."},{"id":"pronoun-A-24","title":"A baker’s words","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"“{I} will hold the bowl,” said the baker.","question":"Who or what does “I” refer to?","options":["the baker","one of the children","the bowl"],"answer":"the baker","hint":"The speaker is named after “said”.","why":"“I” refers to the baker who is speaking.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"pronoun-A-25","title":"Walking in snow","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","passage":"Kwame carried a red sled. {He} walked through the snow.","question":"Who or what does “He” refer to?","options":["Kwame","the sled","the hill"],"answer":"Kwame","hint":"Find the person who carries the sled.","why":"“He” refers to Kwame, who is walking with the sled.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park."},{"id":"pronoun-A-26","title":"Looking in pools","image":"assets/illustrations/rock-pools.webp","passage":"The children found small rock pools. {These} held little sea creatures.","question":"Who or what does “These” refer to?","options":["the rock pools","the children","the buckets"],"answer":"the rock pools","hint":"Which plural things can hold seawater?","why":"“These” refers to the pools between the rocks.","alt":"Two children crouch beside shallow seawater pools between flat coastal rocks at low tide. They look closely at a tiny crab and shells without touching or disturbing them. An attentive adult guide is beside them. Non-slip shoes, stable rock surfaces and gentle daylight."},{"id":"pronoun-A-27","title":"Robot partners","image":"assets/illustrations/robot-partners.webp","passage":"Nia and Arjun checked the robot. It belonged to {them}.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["Nia and Arjun","the robot’s wheels","their teacher alone"],"answer":"Nia and Arjun","hint":"Who built and owns the robot?","why":"“Them” refers to Nia and Arjun, the robot’s two builders.","alt":"Nia, a Black girl with braided hair, and Arjun, a South Asian boy with glasses, check their small wheeled classroom robot on a table. Arjun reconnects a loose low-voltage plug while Nia watches a green indicator light glow. A delighted teacher stands behind. No exposed mains wiring, no labels."},{"id":"pronoun-A-28","title":"A paper glider","image":"assets/illustrations/paper-gliders.webp","passage":"Ben folded a paper glider. {It} landed in a bush.","question":"Who or what does “It” refer to?","options":["the paper glider","Ben","the grass"],"answer":"the paper glider","hint":"What was launched and then landed?","why":"“It” refers to the glider that Ben launched.","alt":"Ben, a red-haired boy, and Maya, a girl with dark braids, test two plain paper gliders on an open grassy lawn. One glider has drifted gently into a low bush while the other rests in Maya's hand. Ben walks toward the bush to retrieve the glider. A coherent outdoor scene with both gliders easy to see."},{"id":"pronoun-A-29","title":"Museum visitors","image":"assets/illustrations/museum-fossil.webp","passage":"“Please show {us} the fossil,” the visitors asked.","question":"Who or what does “us” refer to?","options":["the visitors","the museum guide alone","the fossils"],"answer":"the visitors","hint":"Which group is asking to see something?","why":"The visitors use “us” to mean their own group.","alt":"An adult museum guide shows a large spiral fossil in a low glass display case to a small group of fascinated children. One child uses a manual wheelchair and has a clear view beside the other visitors. A skeleton exhibit is softly visible behind them. No labels or readable signage."},{"id":"pronoun-A-30","title":"Space club","image":"assets/illustrations/space-club.webp","passage":"The club members studied a model. {They} noticed the small planets.","question":"Who or what does “They” refer to?","options":["the club members","the model planets","the table"],"answer":"the club members","hint":"Which group is studying and pointing?","why":"“They” refers to the club members examining the model.","alt":"A diverse group of three children in an after-school space club gathers around a tabletop solar-system model. They point to small colourful planets attached to thin supports around a large central sun. Warm classroom, thoughtful curious expressions, no printed labels or floating text."}],"AA":[{"id":"pronoun-AA-01","title":"The rain cover","image":"assets/illustrations/rain-cover.webp","passage":"Maya and Ben checked the tent before the shower. Maya spread a waterproof cover across the roof. {It} kept rain away from their bedding.","question":"Who or what does “It” refer to?","options":["the waterproof cover","Maya","the bedding"],"answer":"the waterproof cover","hint":"Look for the thing that keeps rain away.","why":"The waterproof cover keeps the bedding dry, so “it” refers to the cover.","alt":"Maya, a brown-skinned girl with two braids, and Ben, a fair-skinned boy with curly red hair, pull a waterproof teal rain cover tightly over an orange tent. Secure pegs and taut ropes are visible. Bedding remains dry inside the tent. A light rain shower falls in the woodland clearing."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-02","title":"The school project","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","passage":"Before the lesson, Lina found a clear space at the desk and opened her notebook. {She} began writing the first line.","question":"Who or what does “She” refer to?","options":["Lina","the notebook","the desk"],"answer":"Lina","hint":"Find the person doing the writing.","why":"“She” refers to Lina, the person who begins writing.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-03","title":"Reading the map","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"Two young hikers stopped beside the path and unfolded a map. {They} traced the route before walking farther.","question":"Who or what does “They” refer to?","options":["the two hikers","the map","the trail"],"answer":"the two hikers","hint":"The pronoun means more than one person.","why":"“They” refers to the two hikers who study the route.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-04","title":"A windy afternoon","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Jamal let out a little more string as the colourful kite rose above the field. He kept his eyes on {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the kite","the field","the string"],"answer":"the kite","hint":"What is rising above the field?","why":"Jamal is watching the kite, so “it” refers to the kite.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-05","title":"At the park","image":"assets/illustrations/park-picnic.webp","passage":"Two friends found a level patch of grass beside the park path. They placed a picnic basket between their bags. The basket belonged to {them}.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["the two friends","the basket","the bags"],"answer":"the two friends","hint":"Find the people who own the basket.","why":"“Them” refers to the two friends, not to their belongings.","alt":"Two friends, a girl with light-brown skin and glasses and a boy with black hair, sit on a clearly spread yellow picnic blanket in a green park. A woven picnic basket sits between their bags. Lunch containers and apple slices are on the blanket. A level grassy patch beside a broad park path."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-06","title":"Ready to sail","image":"assets/illustrations/sailing-ropes.webp","passage":"The instructor finished checking the life jackets and stepped beside the boat. {He} examined the ropes before the lesson.","question":"Who or what does “He” refer to?","options":["the instructor","the boat","the ropes"],"answer":"the instructor","hint":"Which person can examine the ropes?","why":"“He” refers to the instructor who checks the equipment.","alt":"An adult male sailing instructor checks neatly coiled ropes on a small training sailboat beside a sheltered marina dock. Two children in properly fastened life jackets watch attentively. The boat has a prominent pale sail, a safe simple hull and tidy rigging. Calm harbour water and distant colourful boats."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-07","title":"Garden helpers","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","passage":"Sofia set a small bucket beside the vegetable bed. She pulled weeds from the soil and dropped them into {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the bucket","Sofia","the vegetable bed"],"answer":"the bucket","hint":"Find the container used for the weeds.","why":"The bucket is the container, so the highlighted “it” refers to the bucket.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-08","title":"Mixing the batter","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"Mila stood beside the mixing bowl with a spoon in one hand. {Her} apron protected the clothes underneath.","question":"Who or what does “Her” refer to?","options":["Mila","the spoon","the bowl"],"answer":"Mila","hint":"Whose apron protects their clothes?","why":"“Her” means that the apron belongs to Mila.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-09","title":"Science partners","image":"assets/illustrations/science-tray.webp","passage":"Ruby and Min prepared the experiment together at one table. They placed a tray under the cup. {Their} tray caught the drips.","question":"Who or what does “Their” refer to?","options":["Ruby and Min","the cup","the drips"],"answer":"Ruby and Min","hint":"Look for the two people sharing the tray.","why":"“Their” refers to Ruby and Min, who prepared the experiment together.","alt":"Ruby, a fair-skinned girl with auburn hair, and Min, an East Asian boy with glasses, share a classroom science table. Wearing safety goggles, they pour water between clear cups above a shallow tray. A few drops land in the tray, keeping the surrounding table dry. Friendly teacher in the background."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-10","title":"A snowy day","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","passage":"Before touching the cold snow, the children pulled on thick gloves. {These} covered their fingers and kept out the chill.","question":"Who or what does “These” refer to?","options":["the gloves","the children","the snow"],"answer":"the gloves","hint":"Which plural things cover fingers?","why":"“These” refers to the gloves that cover the children’s fingers.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-11","title":"A sandcastle","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"Mei filled two small buckets at the damp edge of the beach. She lifted {them} carefully and carried both to the sandcastle.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["the two buckets","Mei and her friend","the castle walls"],"answer":"the two buckets","hint":"The pronoun refers to the things Mei carries.","why":"“Them” refers to the two buckets Mei lifts and carries.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-12","title":"At the station","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"A family stood together behind the safety line on the platform. {They} watched the track for their approaching train.","question":"Who or what does “They” refer to?","options":["the family members","the platform","the track"],"answer":"the family members","hint":"Which group is waiting for the train?","why":"“They” refers to the family members waiting together.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-13","title":"A thirsty dog","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","passage":"A dog stood beside the clean water bowl with its tongue out. {It} was ready for a drink after the walk.","question":"Who or what does “It” refer to?","options":["the dog","the bowl","the walk"],"answer":"the dog","hint":"What living thing can want a drink?","why":"“It” refers to the thirsty dog.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-14","title":"On the field","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","passage":"Coach Lee gathered the players near the side of the football field. She explained a new passing drill to {them}.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["the players","Coach Lee","the football"],"answer":"the players","hint":"Who receives the coach’s instructions?","why":"“Them” refers to the players listening to the coach.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-15","title":"A book to share","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"Sofia selected a book from the library shelf and placed it on the table. {Its} cover showed a colourful scene.","question":"Who or what does “Its” refer to?","options":["the book","Sofia","the table"],"answer":"the book","hint":"Which thing has a cover?","why":"“Its” means that the cover belongs to the book.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-16","title":"The treehouse plan","image":"assets/illustrations/measuring-board.webp","passage":"The adult builder steadied a long board on the workbench. The children measured {it} before the next step.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the board","the builder","the children"],"answer":"the board","hint":"Find the thing being measured.","why":"The children measure the board, so “it” refers to the board.","alt":"An adult builder steadies a sturdy long wooden board flat on a low workbench while two children carefully measure it with a tape measure. All wear safety glasses. A small partly built treehouse appears safely at ground level behind them. No power tools in use, no readable measurements."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-17","title":"The hiking group","image":"assets/illustrations/night-camp.webp","passage":"The hikers gathered at the start of the path. “{We} will stay together and follow the trail,” they said.","question":"Who or what does “We” refer to?","options":["the hikers","the trail markers","the trees"],"answer":"the hikers","hint":"Who is speaking inside the quotation marks?","why":"The hikers say “we” to mean themselves as a group.","alt":"A small supervised group of young hikers stays together beside their campsite at dusk. A girl uses a torch to illuminate the woodland path, and a boy points toward their glowing tent. The adult guide is close beside them. A gentle moon and stars above; warm, reassuring night scene."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-18","title":"The skateboard","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Finn pointed to the skateboard beside the ramp. “Please leave that board here; it belongs to {me},” he said.","question":"Who or what does “me” refer to?","options":["Finn","his friend","the instructor"],"answer":"Finn","hint":"Read the words that tell you who is speaking.","why":"Finn is speaking, so “me” refers to Finn.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-19","title":"Bridge builders","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"Lina and Andre worked together to build a model bridge from craft sticks. {Their} finished model stood in the centre of the table.","question":"Who or what does “Their” refer to?","options":["Lina and Andre","the craft sticks","the table"],"answer":"Lina and Andre","hint":"Who made and owns the model?","why":"The model belongs to its builders, Lina and Andre.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-20","title":"Bike practice","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"The young rider checked the bicycle before starting. A fitted helmet sat on her head, with its strap fastened under {her} chin.","question":"Who or what does “her” refer to?","options":["the rider","the bicycle","the instructor"],"answer":"the rider","hint":"Find the person wearing the helmet.","why":"“Her” refers to the rider whose chin is under the helmet strap.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-21","title":"Flying together","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"A girl and a boy held the kite string together in the open field. A gust of wind lifted {their} colourful kite.","question":"Who or what does “their” refer to?","options":["the girl and the boy","the nearby trees","the clouds"],"answer":"the girl and the boy","hint":"Which people are sharing the kite?","why":"“Their” refers to the girl and the boy sharing the kite.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-22","title":"Picnic blanket","image":"assets/illustrations/park-picnic.webp","passage":"The children spread a picnic blanket over a dry patch of grass. They placed their lunch beside them and sat on {it}.","question":"Who or what does “it” refer to?","options":["the blanket","their lunch","the tree"],"answer":"the blanket","hint":"Which thing was spread out for sitting?","why":"“It” refers to the blanket spread over the grass.","alt":"Two friends, a girl with light-brown skin and glasses and a boy with black hair, sit on a clearly spread yellow picnic blanket in a green park. A woven picnic basket sits between their bags. Lunch containers and apple slices are on the blanket. A level grassy patch beside a broad park path."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-23","title":"A safe start","image":"assets/illustrations/life-jacket-check.webp","passage":"The sailing instructor checked each child’s life jacket before they boarded. {She} tightened one loose strap and checked the buckle.","question":"Who or what does “She” refer to?","options":["the sailing instructor","a child’s jacket","the boat"],"answer":"the sailing instructor","hint":"Who checks and tightens the strap?","why":"“She” refers to the sailing instructor carrying out the checks.","alt":"An adult female sailing instructor in a navy jacket gently tightens a loose life-jacket strap on a child before boarding a small boat. Show the fitted life jacket and closed buckle prominently. Another child waits wearing a properly fastened life jacket. Calm marina dock, safely away from the edge."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-24","title":"A baker’s words","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"The adult baker stood beside the children at the kitchen counter. “{I} will hold the bowl while you stir,” said the baker.","question":"Who or what does “I” refer to?","options":["the baker","one of the children","the bowl"],"answer":"the baker","hint":"The speaker is named after “said”.","why":"“I” refers to the baker who is speaking.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-25","title":"Walking in snow","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","passage":"Kwame picked up the red sled at the edge of the snowy path. {He} carried it toward the gentle hill.","question":"Who or what does “He” refer to?","options":["Kwame","the sled","the hill"],"answer":"Kwame","hint":"Find the person who carries the sled.","why":"“He” refers to Kwame, who is walking with the sled.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-26","title":"Looking in pools","image":"assets/illustrations/rock-pools.webp","passage":"At low tide, the children discovered several small pools between the rocks. {These} held seawater and tiny creatures.","question":"Who or what does “These” refer to?","options":["the rock pools","the children","the buckets"],"answer":"the rock pools","hint":"Which plural things can hold seawater?","why":"“These” refers to the pools between the rocks.","alt":"Two children crouch beside shallow seawater pools between flat coastal rocks at low tide. They look closely at a tiny crab and shells without touching or disturbing them. An attentive adult guide is beside them. Non-slip shoes, stable rock surfaces and gentle daylight."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-27","title":"Robot partners","image":"assets/illustrations/robot-partners.webp","passage":"Nia and Arjun had built the small robot together. After checking its wheels, they explained that it belonged to {them}.","question":"Who or what does “them” refer to?","options":["Nia and Arjun","the robot’s wheels","their teacher alone"],"answer":"Nia and Arjun","hint":"Who built and owns the robot?","why":"“Them” refers to Nia and Arjun, the robot’s two builders.","alt":"Nia, a Black girl with braided hair, and Arjun, a South Asian boy with glasses, check their small wheeled classroom robot on a table. Arjun reconnects a loose low-voltage plug while Nia watches a green indicator light glow. A delighted teacher stands behind. No exposed mains wiring, no labels."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-28","title":"A paper glider","image":"assets/illustrations/paper-gliders.webp","passage":"Ben pressed the final fold in a paper glider and launched it across the grass. {It} drifted sideways and landed in a bush.","question":"Who or what does “It” refer to?","options":["the paper glider","Ben","the grass"],"answer":"the paper glider","hint":"What was launched and then landed?","why":"“It” refers to the glider that Ben launched.","alt":"Ben, a red-haired boy, and Maya, a girl with dark braids, test two plain paper gliders on an open grassy lawn. One glider has drifted gently into a low bush while the other rests in Maya's hand. Ben walks toward the bush to retrieve the glider. A coherent outdoor scene with both gliders easy to see."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-29","title":"Museum visitors","image":"assets/illustrations/museum-fossil.webp","passage":"The visitors gathered beside the museum guide. “Please show {us} the fossil in this case,” the visitors asked.","question":"Who or what does “us” refer to?","options":["the visitors","the museum guide alone","the fossils"],"answer":"the visitors","hint":"Which group is asking to see something?","why":"The visitors use “us” to mean their own group.","alt":"An adult museum guide shows a large spiral fossil in a low glass display case to a small group of fascinated children. One child uses a manual wheelchair and has a clear view beside the other visitors. A skeleton exhibit is softly visible behind them. No labels or readable signage."},{"id":"pronoun-AA-30","title":"Space club","image":"assets/illustrations/space-club.webp","passage":"The space-club members gathered around the model on the table. {They} took turns pointing out the smaller planets.","question":"Who or what does “They” refer to?","options":["the club members","the model planets","the table"],"answer":"the club members","hint":"Which group is studying and pointing?","why":"“They” refers to the club members examining the model.","alt":"A diverse group of three children in an after-school space club gathers around a tabletop solar-system model. They point to small colourful planets attached to thin supports around a large central sun. Warm classroom, thoughtful curious expressions, no printed labels or floating text."}]},"homophone":{"A":[{"id":"homophone-A-01","title":"Ready for school","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","passage":"Lina walked {___} the classroom.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["to","too","two"],"answer":"to","hint":"Look for a word showing where Lina is going.","why":"“To” shows direction toward a place.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words."},{"id":"homophone-A-02","title":"Joining the fun","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Jamal wanted to fly the kite {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["too","to","two"],"answer":"too","hint":"The missing word means “also”.","why":"“Too” means “also” in this sentence.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"homophone-A-03","title":"Glider partners","image":"assets/illustrations/paper-gliders.webp","passage":"One glider for Maya and one for Ben made {___} gliders.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["two","to","too"],"answer":"two","hint":"Count one for each of the two children.","why":"“Two” is the number that tells how many gliders there were.","alt":"Ben, a red-haired boy, and Maya, a girl with dark braids, test two plain paper gliders on an open grassy lawn. One glider has drifted gently into a low bush while the other rests in Maya's hand. Ben walks toward the bush to retrieve the glider. A coherent outdoor scene with both gliders easy to see."},{"id":"homophone-A-04","title":"Bridge partners","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"Lina and Andre showed {___} model.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["their","there","they’re"],"answer":"their","hint":"The model belongs to the two children.","why":"“Their” shows that the model belongs to Lina and Andre.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"homophone-A-05","title":"At the library","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"“Put the book over {___},” said Sofia.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["there","their","they’re"],"answer":"there","hint":"Sofia is pointing to a place.","why":"“There” names the place where the book should go.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"homophone-A-06","title":"On the trail","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers know the path. {___} ready to begin.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["They’re","Their","There"],"answer":"They’re","hint":"Try replacing the word with “they are”.","why":"“They’re” is the short form of “they are”.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"homophone-A-07","title":"Helmet check","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"“Fasten {___} helmet,” said the instructor.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["your","you’re"],"answer":"your","hint":"The helmet belongs to the person being spoken to.","why":"“Your” shows whose helmet it is.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"homophone-A-08","title":"A good pass","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","passage":"“{___} ready to pass,” said the coach.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["You’re","Your"],"answer":"You’re","hint":"Try the two words “you are”.","why":"“You’re” means “you are”.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline."},{"id":"homophone-A-09","title":"A station sound","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"The family could {___} the train arrive.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["hear","here"],"answer":"hear","hint":"The clue is a sound reaching their ears.","why":"“Hear” means to notice a sound with your ears.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"homophone-A-10","title":"Meeting place","image":"assets/illustrations/jeep-trail.webp","passage":"“Please wait {___} by the jeep,” said the guide.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["here","hear"],"answer":"here","hint":"The guide is naming the place where people should wait.","why":"“Here” refers to this place.","alt":"A family pauses in a stationary open-top safari jeep on a rough stony woodland track. The child in the back seat touches the smooth padded seat beside them; all occupants wear correctly fastened seat belts. An adult driver holds a map at the meeting point. No traffic danger, no readable plate or signs."},{"id":"homophone-A-11","title":"At the beach","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"The waves rolled in from the {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["sea","see"],"answer":"sea","hint":"The missing word names a body of salt water.","why":"“Sea” names the salty water beside the beach.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."},{"id":"homophone-A-12","title":"Looking carefully","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers used binoculars to {___} a bird.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["see","sea"],"answer":"see","hint":"Binoculars help your eyes do something.","why":"“See” means to notice something with your eyes.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"homophone-A-13","title":"A notebook page","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","passage":"Lina picked up a pencil to {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["write","right"],"answer":"write","hint":"The pencil will make words on the page.","why":"“Write” means to form letters or words.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words."},{"id":"homophone-A-14","title":"Following the map","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The next turn was to the {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["right","write"],"answer":"right","hint":"The sentence names a direction.","why":"“Right” is the direction opposite left.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"homophone-A-15","title":"Baking day","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"The baker measured some {___} into the bowl.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["flour","flower"],"answer":"flour","hint":"Choose the baking ingredient.","why":"“Flour” is the powder used for baking.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"homophone-A-16","title":"In the garden","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","passage":"A bee landed on a {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["flower","flour"],"answer":"flower","hint":"The clue is “petals”.","why":"“Flower” names the part of a plant that has petals.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands."},{"id":"homophone-A-17","title":"Getting ready","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Finn put on a {___} of knee pads.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["pair","pear"],"answer":"pair","hint":"The sentence means two matching things.","why":"“Pair” means two things used together.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"homophone-A-18","title":"A windy kite","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"A gust {___} the kite upward.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["blew","blue"],"answer":"blew","hint":"Choose the action done by the wind.","why":"“Blew” tells what the moving wind did.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"homophone-A-19","title":"Making a model","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"Andre added one more {___} of wood.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["piece","peace"],"answer":"piece","hint":"The sentence means one part of a larger material.","why":"“Piece” means a part or portion of something.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"homophone-A-20","title":"A happy dog","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","passage":"The dog wagged its {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["tail","tale"],"answer":"tail","hint":"Choose the body part a dog can wag.","why":"“Tail” is the body part at the back of the dog.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them."},{"id":"homophone-A-21","title":"On the water","image":"assets/illustrations/sailing-ropes.webp","passage":"The wind filled the boat’s {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["sail","sale"],"answer":"sail","hint":"Choose the piece of fabric on the boat.","why":"“Sail” is the fabric that catches the wind to help move a boat.","alt":"An adult male sailing instructor checks neatly coiled ropes on a small training sailboat beside a sheltered marina dock. Two children in properly fastened life jackets watch attentively. The boat has a prominent pale sail, a safe simple hull and tidy rigging. Calm harbour water and distant colourful boats."},{"id":"homophone-A-22","title":"After sunset","image":"assets/illustrations/night-camp.webp","passage":"The campers used a flashlight at {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["night","knight"],"answer":"night","hint":"The clue is that the sun has set.","why":"“Night” is the dark part of the day after sunset.","alt":"A small supervised group of young hikers stays together beside their campsite at dusk. A girl uses a torch to illuminate the woodland path, and a boy points toward their glowing tent. The adult guide is close beside them. A gentle moon and stars above; warm, reassuring night scene."},{"id":"homophone-A-23","title":"Picnic break","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Jamal {___} his lunch before flying the kite.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["ate","eight"],"answer":"ate","hint":"Choose the past-tense action for eating.","why":"“Ate” is the past tense of “eat”.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"homophone-A-24","title":"A garden visitor","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","passage":"A {___} buzzed beside the flowers.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["bee","be"],"answer":"bee","hint":"Choose the insect that buzzes.","why":"“Bee” names the buzzing insect.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands."},{"id":"homophone-A-25","title":"Bike safety","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"The rider squeezed the {___} to slow down.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["brake","break"],"answer":"brake","hint":"Choose the bicycle part used to slow or stop.","why":"“Brake” is the device that slows or stops a bicycle.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"homophone-A-26","title":"A bicycle ride","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"Sofia {___} her bicycle along the path.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["rode","road"],"answer":"rode","hint":"The sentence needs an action, not a place.","why":"“Rode” is the past tense of “ride”.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"homophone-A-27","title":"Reading time","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"The teacher read the story {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["aloud","allowed"],"answer":"aloud","hint":"The clue is a voice that everyone can hear.","why":"“Aloud” means using your voice so others can hear.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"homophone-A-28","title":"Winter clothes","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","passage":"The children would {___} warm coats.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["wear","where"],"answer":"wear","hint":"Choose the action of putting clothes on your body.","why":"“Wear” means to have clothing on your body.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park."},{"id":"homophone-A-29","title":"Meeting at the library","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"The friends planned to {___} at the library.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["meet","meat"],"answer":"meet","hint":"Choose the action of coming together.","why":"“Meet” means to come together. “Meat” is a type of food.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"homophone-A-30","title":"A beach trip","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"The friends hoped for sunny {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["weather","whether"],"answer":"weather","hint":"Choose the word for outdoor conditions.","why":"“Weather” means outdoor conditions such as sunshine, rain or wind.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."}],"AA":[{"id":"homophone-AA-01","title":"Ready for school","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","passage":"Lina carried her notebook down the hall on her way {___} the classroom.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["to","too","two"],"answer":"to","hint":"Look for a word showing where Lina is going.","why":"“To” shows direction toward a place.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words."},{"id":"homophone-AA-02","title":"Joining the fun","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Asha had a turn holding the string, and Jamal wanted a turn {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["too","to","two"],"answer":"too","hint":"The missing word means “also”.","why":"“Too” means “also” in this sentence.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"homophone-AA-03","title":"Glider partners","image":"assets/illustrations/paper-gliders.webp","passage":"Maya folded one glider and Ben folded another, so together they had {___} gliders.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["two","to","too"],"answer":"two","hint":"Count one for each of the two children.","why":"“Two” is the number that tells how many gliders there were.","alt":"Ben, a red-haired boy, and Maya, a girl with dark braids, test two plain paper gliders on an open grassy lawn. One glider has drifted gently into a low bush while the other rests in Maya's hand. Ben walks toward the bush to retrieve the glider. A coherent outdoor scene with both gliders easy to see."},{"id":"homophone-AA-04","title":"Bridge partners","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"After working together, Lina and Andre proudly showed {___} model to the class.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["their","there","they’re"],"answer":"their","hint":"The model belongs to the two children.","why":"“Their” shows that the model belongs to Lina and Andre.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"homophone-AA-05","title":"At the library","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"Sofia pointed to a clear space at the far end of the table. “Put the book over {___},” she said.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["there","their","they’re"],"answer":"there","hint":"Sofia is pointing to a place.","why":"“There” names the place where the book should go.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"homophone-AA-06","title":"On the trail","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers have checked the map and filled their water bottles. {___} ready to begin.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["They’re","Their","There"],"answer":"They’re","hint":"Try replacing the word with “they are”.","why":"“They’re” is the short form of “they are”.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"homophone-AA-07","title":"Helmet check","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"Before the bike ride, the instructor said, “Fasten {___} helmet and check the strap.”","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["your","you’re"],"answer":"your","hint":"The helmet belongs to the person being spoken to.","why":"“Your” shows whose helmet it is.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"homophone-AA-08","title":"A good pass","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","passage":"The player looked up and spotted a teammate. “{___} ready to pass now,” said the coach.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["You’re","Your"],"answer":"You’re","hint":"Try the two words “you are”.","why":"“You’re” means “you are”.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline."},{"id":"homophone-AA-09","title":"A station sound","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"Before the train came into view, the family could {___} its wheels on the track.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["hear","here"],"answer":"hear","hint":"The clue is a sound reaching their ears.","why":"“Hear” means to notice a sound with your ears.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"homophone-AA-10","title":"Meeting place","image":"assets/illustrations/jeep-trail.webp","passage":"The guide pointed to the safe space beside the parked jeep. “Please wait {___},” he said.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["here","hear"],"answer":"here","hint":"The guide is naming the place where people should wait.","why":"“Here” refers to this place.","alt":"A family pauses in a stationary open-top safari jeep on a rough stony woodland track. The child in the back seat touches the smooth padded seat beside them; all occupants wear correctly fastened seat belts. An adult driver holds a map at the meeting point. No traffic danger, no readable plate or signs."},{"id":"homophone-AA-11","title":"At the beach","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"Beyond the sandcastle, salty waves rolled toward the shore from the {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["sea","see"],"answer":"sea","hint":"The missing word names a body of salt water.","why":"“Sea” names the salty water beside the beach.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."},{"id":"homophone-AA-12","title":"Looking carefully","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"A bird rested far away on a branch, so the hikers used binoculars to {___} it clearly.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["see","sea"],"answer":"see","hint":"Binoculars help your eyes do something.","why":"“See” means to notice something with your eyes.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"homophone-AA-13","title":"A notebook page","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","passage":"Lina opened a clean page and picked up a pencil to {___} her first sentence.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["write","right"],"answer":"write","hint":"The pencil will make words on the page.","why":"“Write” means to form letters or words.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words."},{"id":"homophone-AA-14","title":"Following the map","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The arrow on the map pointed away from the left path; the next turn was to the {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["right","write"],"answer":"right","hint":"The sentence names a direction.","why":"“Right” is the direction opposite left.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"homophone-AA-15","title":"Baking day","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"The baker measured the dry white {___} before adding milk and stirring the cake batter.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["flour","flower"],"answer":"flour","hint":"Choose the baking ingredient.","why":"“Flour” is the powder used for baking.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"homophone-AA-16","title":"In the garden","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","passage":"Beside the vegetable bed, a bee landed on the bright petals of a {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["flower","flour"],"answer":"flower","hint":"The clue is “petals”.","why":"“Flower” names the part of a plant that has petals.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands."},{"id":"homophone-AA-17","title":"Getting ready","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Before using the skateboard, Finn put on a matching {___} of knee pads, one for each knee.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["pair","pear"],"answer":"pair","hint":"The sentence means two matching things.","why":"“Pair” means two things used together.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"homophone-AA-18","title":"A windy kite","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Jamal held the string tightly when a sudden gust {___} the kite upward.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["blew","blue"],"answer":"blew","hint":"Choose the action done by the wind.","why":"“Blew” tells what the moving wind did.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"homophone-AA-19","title":"Making a model","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"The model bridge needed another support, so Andre added one more small {___} of wood.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["piece","peace"],"answer":"piece","hint":"The sentence means one part of a larger material.","why":"“Piece” means a part or portion of something.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"homophone-AA-20","title":"A happy dog","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","passage":"When its friend came home, the happy dog wagged its {___} beside the water bowl.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["tail","tale"],"answer":"tail","hint":"Choose the body part a dog can wag.","why":"“Tail” is the body part at the back of the dog.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them."},{"id":"homophone-AA-21","title":"On the water","image":"assets/illustrations/sailing-ropes.webp","passage":"The instructor adjusted the rope so the wind could fill the boat’s white {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["sail","sale"],"answer":"sail","hint":"Choose the piece of fabric on the boat.","why":"“Sail” is the fabric that catches the wind to help move a boat.","alt":"An adult male sailing instructor checks neatly coiled ropes on a small training sailboat beside a sheltered marina dock. Two children in properly fastened life jackets watch attentively. The boat has a prominent pale sail, a safe simple hull and tidy rigging. Calm harbour water and distant colourful boats."},{"id":"homophone-AA-22","title":"After sunset","image":"assets/illustrations/night-camp.webp","passage":"The sun had set behind the trees, so the campers used a flashlight at {___}.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["night","knight"],"answer":"night","hint":"The clue is that the sun has set.","why":"“Night” is the dark part of the day after sunset.","alt":"A small supervised group of young hikers stays together beside their campsite at dusk. A girl uses a torch to illuminate the woodland path, and a boy points toward their glowing tent. The adult guide is close beside them. A gentle moon and stars above; warm, reassuring night scene."},{"id":"homophone-AA-23","title":"Picnic break","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Before returning to the kite string, Jamal sat on the picnic blanket and {___} his lunch.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["ate","eight"],"answer":"ate","hint":"Choose the past-tense action for eating.","why":"“Ate” is the past tense of “eat”.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"homophone-AA-24","title":"A garden visitor","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","passage":"The children heard a gentle buzzing as a {___} moved from one flower to another.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["bee","be"],"answer":"bee","hint":"Choose the insect that buzzes.","why":"“Bee” names the buzzing insect.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands."},{"id":"homophone-AA-25","title":"Bike safety","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"As the bicycle approached the practice line, the rider squeezed the {___} lever to slow down.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["brake","break"],"answer":"brake","hint":"Choose the bicycle part used to slow or stop.","why":"“Brake” is the device that slows or stops a bicycle.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"homophone-AA-26","title":"A bicycle ride","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"With her helmet fastened, Sofia {___} her bicycle along the smooth practice path.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["rode","road"],"answer":"rode","hint":"The sentence needs an action, not a place.","why":"“Rode” is the past tense of “ride”.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"homophone-AA-27","title":"Reading time","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"The children listened while the teacher read the story {___}, using a clear voice everyone could hear.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["aloud","allowed"],"answer":"aloud","hint":"The clue is a voice that everyone can hear.","why":"“Aloud” means using your voice so others can hear.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"homophone-AA-28","title":"Winter clothes","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","passage":"Before going outside into the snow, the children would {___} warm coats and gloves.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["wear","where"],"answer":"wear","hint":"Choose the action of putting clothes on your body.","why":"“Wear” means to have clothing on your body.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park."},{"id":"homophone-AA-29","title":"Meeting at the library","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"After lunch, the friends planned to {___} beside the library’s reading table.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["meet","meat"],"answer":"meet","hint":"Choose the action of coming together.","why":"“Meet” means to come together. “Meat” is a type of food.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."},{"id":"homophone-AA-30","title":"A beach trip","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"The friends packed their beach bag and hoped the {___} would stay warm and sunny.","question":"Which word completes the sentence?","options":["weather","whether"],"answer":"weather","hint":"Choose the word for outdoor conditions.","why":"“Weather” means outdoor conditions such as sunshine, rain or wind.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."}]},"paragraph":{"A":[{"id":"paragraph-A-01","title":"Keeping a tent dry","image":"assets/illustrations/rain-cover.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A rain cover helps keep a tent dry.","It stops rain from reaching the bedding.","The campers have a dry place to sleep.","The tent has pockets for small things."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on keeping rain away from the bedding. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on keeping rain away from the bedding. The pockets store things; they do not keep rain away from the bedding.","alt":"Maya, a brown-skinned girl with two braids, and Ben, a fair-skinned boy with curly red hair, pull a waterproof teal rain cover tightly over an orange tent. Secure pegs and taut ropes are visible. Bedding remains dry inside the tent. A light rain shower falls in the woodland clearing.","focus":"keeping rain away from the bedding"},{"id":"paragraph-A-02","title":"Reading a trail map","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Hikers use a map to choose their route.","Its marked paths show the way to the campsite.","The group can follow the route they have chosen.","The hikers carry snacks in their backpacks."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on using map markings to choose a route. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using map markings to choose a route. Carrying snacks is part of a hike, but it does not explain finding a route on a map.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze.","focus":"using map markings to choose a route"},{"id":"paragraph-A-03","title":"Getting ready to write","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Lina gets her desk ready before she writes.","She opens her notebook to a clean page.","Now she has a clear place to begin.","Lina writes about a trip to the park."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on preparing a writing space. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on preparing a writing space. The trip is the subject of Lina’s writing. The paragraph is about getting her desk ready.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words.","focus":"preparing a writing space"},{"id":"paragraph-A-04","title":"Fitting a bicycle helmet","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A bicycle helmet needs to fit properly.","Its straps fasten firmly under the rider’s chin.","The helmet can then stay in place during the ride.","The rider rings the bicycle bell on the path."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on making sure a helmet fits properly. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on making sure a helmet fits properly. Ringing a bell concerns using the bicycle, rather than fitting the helmet.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety.","focus":"making sure a helmet fits properly"},{"id":"paragraph-A-05","title":"Choosing a kite-flying space","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A kite needs a clear place to fly.","An open field gives it room to rise.","Choosing enough space is a good start.","Some kites are made from thin paper."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on choosing a clear place to fly a kite. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on choosing a clear place to fly a kite. The paper tells us what a kite is made from, rather than where to fly it.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space.","focus":"choosing a clear place to fly a kite"},{"id":"paragraph-A-06","title":"Preparing a picnic spot","image":"assets/illustrations/park-picnic.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["The friends prepare a picnic spot for lunch.","They spread a blanket on a dry patch of grass.","Now they have a comfortable place to eat.","The friends wave to a dog on the path."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on getting a comfortable place ready for lunch. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on getting a comfortable place ready for lunch. Waving to the dog does not help prepare the place where the friends will eat.","alt":"Two friends, a girl with light-brown skin and glasses and a boy with black hair, sit on a clearly spread yellow picnic blanket in a green park. A woven picnic basket sits between their bags. Lunch containers and apple slices are on the blanket. A level grassy patch beside a broad park path.","focus":"getting a comfortable place ready for lunch"},{"id":"paragraph-A-07","title":"Preparing to sail","image":"assets/illustrations/sailing-ropes.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Sailors check their equipment before leaving.","The instructor looks closely at the ropes.","These checks help the group begin safely.","The sailors practise turning the boat."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on checking equipment before the sailing lesson. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on checking equipment before the sailing lesson. Practising a turn is a sailing skill. The paragraph is about checking equipment before setting off.","alt":"An adult male sailing instructor checks neatly coiled ropes on a small training sailboat beside a sheltered marina dock. Two children in properly fastened life jackets watch attentively. The boat has a prominent pale sail, a safe simple hull and tidy rigging. Calm harbour water and distant colourful boats.","focus":"checking equipment before the sailing lesson"},{"id":"paragraph-A-08","title":"A safe first dive","image":"assets/illustrations/shallow-dive.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Beginners learn to dive with help close by.","An instructor stays beside them in shallow water.","The children can practise with support nearby.","Small fish swim above the sandy bottom."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on safe conditions for a beginner diving lesson. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on safe conditions for a beginner diving lesson. The fish describe the underwater setting, rather than the support that helps beginners learn safely.","alt":"An adult scuba instructor supervises two children during a beginner lesson in clear shallow water above a sandy seabed. All have coherent fitted scuba gear, masks, regulators and air tanks. Sunlight reaches the visible bottom. Calm close supervision, no animals touched and no deep-water danger.","focus":"safe conditions for a beginner diving lesson"},{"id":"paragraph-A-09","title":"Removing garden weeds","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Pulling weeds gives vegetables more room.","Sofia lifts the weeds out of the garden bed.","The vegetables have less crowding around them.","A yellow flower grows beside the garden path."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on giving vegetable plants room by removing weeds. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on giving vegetable plants room by removing weeds. The flower describes another part of the garden, rather than removing weeds from the vegetable bed.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands.","focus":"giving vegetable plants room by removing weeds"},{"id":"paragraph-A-10","title":"Mixing cake batter","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Stirring brings cake ingredients together.","A spoon mixes them inside the bowl.","The batter is ready for the next baking step.","The cake will cool on a wire rack."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on bringing ingredients together in the mixing bowl. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on bringing ingredients together in the mixing bowl. Cooling happens later. The paragraph explains mixing the ingredients in the bowl.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin.","focus":"bringing ingredients together in the mixing bowl"},{"id":"paragraph-A-11","title":"Preparing a science workspace","image":"assets/illustrations/science-tray.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A tray helps keep a science table tidy.","It catches drips underneath the cups.","The table stays cleaner while the children work.","The children draw what they see in the cup."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on keeping the experiment’s workspace clear and tidy. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on keeping the experiment’s workspace clear and tidy. Drawing records what happens in the cup, rather than keeping the work area tidy.","alt":"Ruby, a fair-skinned girl with auburn hair, and Min, an East Asian boy with glasses, share a classroom science table. Wearing safety goggles, they pour water between clear cups above a shallow tray. A few drops land in the tray, keeping the surrounding table dry. Friendly teacher in the background.","focus":"keeping the experiment’s workspace clear and tidy"},{"id":"paragraph-A-12","title":"Dressing for snow","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Warm clothes help children enjoy snowy weather.","Gloves cover their hands in the cold.","The children can play more comfortably.","The children choose a place to build a snowman."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on choosing clothes that keep the body warm. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on choosing clothes that keep the body warm. Choosing a snowman spot is a play activity, rather than a choice about warm clothing.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park.","focus":"choosing clothes that keep the body warm"},{"id":"paragraph-A-13","title":"Shaping a sandcastle","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Simple tools help shape a sandcastle.","A bucket forms towers from damp sand.","The builders can use tools to add more shapes.","A shell will decorate the top of the castle."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on using tools to form the castle’s main shapes. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using tools to form the castle’s main shapes. The shell decorates the castle. It is not a tool for shaping the sand.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby.","focus":"using tools to form the castle’s main shapes"},{"id":"paragraph-A-14","title":"Waiting safely at a station","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Passengers wait safely on the station platform.","They stand behind the platform’s safety line.","They stay clear of the edge while the train arrives.","Passengers buy tickets before reaching the platform."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on waiting safely on the platform. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on waiting safely on the platform. Buying a ticket is another part of a train journey, rather than a rule for waiting safely on the platform.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print.","focus":"waiting safely on the platform"},{"id":"paragraph-A-15","title":"Fresh water for a dog","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Dogs need fresh drinking water.","A clean bowl holds it where the dog can reach it.","Checking the bowl helps the dog get a drink.","The dog likes to play fetch after its walk."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on making fresh drinking water available to a dog. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on making fresh drinking water available to a dog. Playing fetch is part of the dog’s day, rather than providing drinking water.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them.","focus":"making fresh drinking water available to a dog"},{"id":"paragraph-A-16","title":"Passing as a team","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Passing helps football players share the ball.","A careful pass sends it to a teammate.","Working together keeps the ball moving between players.","A player stretches before running onto the field."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on moving the ball between football teammates. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on moving the ball between football teammates. Stretching prepares a player’s body, rather than moving the ball between teammates.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline.","focus":"moving the ball between football teammates"},{"id":"paragraph-A-17","title":"Choosing a library book","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A reader looks for clues when choosing a book.","The cover gives a first idea of the story inside.","These clues help the reader decide what to read.","The librarian stamps a return date inside the book."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on using clues from a book to decide whether to read it. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using clues from a book to decide whether to read it. The stamp tells the reader when to return the book, rather than what its story is like.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages.","focus":"using clues from a book to decide whether to read it"},{"id":"paragraph-A-18","title":"Building safely with an adult","image":"assets/illustrations/measuring-board.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Children build a treehouse with adult guidance.","An adult handles tools that are unsafe for children.","The children can learn while working safely.","The finished treehouse will have a green roof."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on working safely with adult guidance. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on working safely with adult guidance. The roof’s colour concerns appearance, rather than working safely with an adult.","alt":"An adult builder steadies a sturdy long wooden board flat on a low workbench while two children carefully measure it with a tape measure. All wear safety glasses. A small partly built treehouse appears safely at ground level behind them. No power tools in use, no readable measurements.","focus":"working safely with adult guidance"},{"id":"paragraph-A-19","title":"A strong model bridge","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A model bridge needs a strong frame.","The builders join craft sticks to support the crossing.","The joined pieces help the bridge stand firmly.","The builders paint small stars on the bridge."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on building the parts that support a model bridge. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on building the parts that support a model bridge. The stars decorate the model, rather than helping to hold it up.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby.","focus":"building the parts that support a model bridge"},{"id":"paragraph-A-20","title":"Sharing mixing jobs","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Baking helpers can share the mixing jobs.","One holds the bowl while another stirs.","Both helpers have a useful task.","The batter is pale yellow in the bowl."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on sharing the jobs during mixing. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on sharing the jobs during mixing. The colour describes the batter, rather than the jobs the helpers share.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin.","focus":"sharing the jobs during mixing"},{"id":"paragraph-A-21","title":"Watching wildlife from a distance","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Binoculars help hikers see distant wildlife.","The lenses make faraway details look larger.","The hikers can watch without getting too close.","The hikers’ boots leave prints in the mud."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on using binoculars to see distant wildlife. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using binoculars to see distant wildlife. The footprints describe the walk, rather than how binoculars help the hikers see wildlife.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze.","focus":"using binoculars to see distant wildlife"},{"id":"paragraph-A-22","title":"Making a snowman’s base","image":"assets/illustrations/snowman.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A large snowball makes a snowman’s base.","Rolling it across fresh snow makes it grow.","The builders have a strong start for their snowman.","A carrot makes a bright nose for the snowman."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on forming a base that can support a snowman. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on forming a base that can support a snowman. The carrot forms a face detail, rather than the base supporting the snowman.","alt":"Two children in warm coats, gloves and boots roll a very large snowball across level snow to build a snowman. A smaller ball waits nearby, with a carrot and two plain pebbles in a basket. The giant lower ball is clearly much larger than their smaller snowballs. Joyful sunny winter park.","focus":"forming a base that can support a snowman"},{"id":"paragraph-A-23","title":"Talking about a shared story","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Friends can work out a story together.","They talk about the pictures to follow what happens.","Sharing ideas helps them understand the story.","They carry the book in a waterproof bag."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on understanding a story by discussing it together. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on understanding a story by discussing it together. The bag protects the book. It does not help the friends discuss what the story means.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages.","focus":"understanding a story by discussing it together"},{"id":"paragraph-A-24","title":"Magnifying a leaf","image":"assets/illustrations/leaf-study.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf.","Its lens makes tiny lines look larger.","The leaf itself stays the same size.","The leaf turns yellow when the season changes."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on how a magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on how a magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf. The colour changes in the leaf itself. The paragraph explains how a lens changes our view of it.","alt":"Two children study a green leaf at a classroom light table. One child holds a magnifying glass over the leaf's clearly visible veins; the other holds a transparent plastic sheet partly across the leaf so it remains visible through the clear material. Careful natural hand poses, a simple uncluttered science table.","focus":"how a magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf"},{"id":"paragraph-A-25","title":"Checking a robot’s connection","image":"assets/illustrations/robot-partners.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A loose plug can stop a small robot from working.","Nia checks the plug and connects it firmly.","The green light shows the connection is working.","The robot’s wheels help it turn around."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on checking an electrical connection in a robot. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on checking an electrical connection in a robot. The wheels explain movement, rather than checking whether a plug is connected.","alt":"Nia, a Black girl with braided hair, and Arjun, a South Asian boy with glasses, check their small wheeled classroom robot on a table. Arjun reconnects a loose low-voltage plug while Nia watches a green indicator light glow. A delighted teacher stands behind. No exposed mains wiring, no labels.","focus":"checking an electrical connection in a robot"},{"id":"paragraph-A-26","title":"Comparing glider landings","image":"assets/illustrations/paper-gliders.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Glider landings give the flyers results to compare.","One glider reaches the grass and another lands in a bush.","The flyers compare where the two gliders finish.","The gliders are made from folded sheets of paper."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on comparing where gliders land in a flight test. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on comparing where gliders land in a flight test. The paper sentence explains how the gliders are made, rather than where they land.","alt":"Ben, a red-haired boy, and Maya, a girl with dark braids, test two plain paper gliders on an open grassy lawn. One glider has drifted gently into a low bush while the other rests in Maya's hand. Ben walks toward the bush to retrieve the glider. A coherent outdoor scene with both gliders easy to see.","focus":"comparing where gliders land in a flight test"},{"id":"paragraph-A-27","title":"Spotting a ready basketball teammate","image":"assets/illustrations/basketball-pass.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A passer looks for a teammate who is ready.","Empty raised hands show a chance to pass.","The ball can move to the waiting teammate.","The basketball net hangs high above the court."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on noticing that a teammate is ready to catch a pass. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on noticing that a teammate is ready to catch a pass. The net describes the court, rather than a teammate’s readiness to catch a pass.","alt":"Two children practise a basketball chest pass on an outdoor court. One girl stands ready with bent knees and open hands while a boy gently passes the basketball toward her. A female coach supervises nearby. Realistic readable body positions, one ball and safe spacing.","focus":"noticing that a teammate is ready to catch a pass"},{"id":"paragraph-A-28","title":"Brushing a pony safely","image":"assets/illustrations/pony-care.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A pony’s coat should be brushed gently.","A suitable brush lifts dust out of the coat.","Careful brushing keeps the coat clean and comfortable.","The pony eats hay from a net in its stall."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on cleaning a pony’s coat through gentle, supervised brushing. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on cleaning a pony’s coat through gentle, supervised brushing. Eating hay concerns feeding, rather than brushing the pony’s coat.","alt":"Priya, a South Asian girl wearing a fitted riding helmet and closed riding boots, gently brushes a calm brown pony's bare back in a stable aisle. An adult instructor holds the pony's lead rope. A saddle waits separately on a stand, clearly not yet on the pony. Warm calm light.","focus":"cleaning a pony’s coat through gentle, supervised brushing"},{"id":"paragraph-A-29","title":"Studying a museum display","image":"assets/illustrations/museum-fossil.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Visitors study a museum display to learn about it.","A guide helps explain details they can see.","Looking and listening help them understand the display.","The display case is locked when the museum closes."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on using observation and a guide to understand a display. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using observation and a guide to understand a display. Locking the case concerns security, rather than learning by looking and listening.","alt":"An adult museum guide shows a large spiral fossil in a low glass display case to a small group of fascinated children. One child uses a manual wheelchair and has a clear view beside the other visitors. A skeleton exhibit is softly visible behind them. No labels or readable signage.","focus":"using observation and a guide to understand a display"},{"id":"paragraph-A-30","title":"Discussing a space model","image":"assets/illustrations/space-club.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A space model helps children share their ideas.","They point to the model planets as they explain.","The group has one display to talk about together.","The model planets are made from painted foam."],"orders":[[0,1,2]],"hint":"Focus on using a shared model to explain ideas to one another. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using a shared model to explain ideas to one another. The foam tells us what the model is made from, rather than how the group uses it to share ideas.","alt":"A diverse group of three children in an after-school space club gathers around a tabletop solar-system model. They point to small colourful planets attached to thin supports around a large central sun. Warm classroom, thoughtful curious expressions, no printed labels or floating text.","focus":"using a shared model to explain ideas to one another"}],"AA":[{"id":"paragraph-AA-01","title":"Keeping a tent dry","image":"assets/illustrations/rain-cover.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A rain cover keeps water away from a tent’s sleeping space.","Its sloping surface directs rain away from the bedding.","Secure pegs keep the cover stretched over the tent.","A well-fitted cover helps the sleeping space stay dry.","A mesh panel lets fresh air move through the tent."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on keeping rain away from the bedding. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on keeping rain away from the bedding. The mesh panel provides fresh air. This paragraph explains protection from rain.","alt":"Maya, a brown-skinned girl with two braids, and Ben, a fair-skinned boy with curly red hair, pull a waterproof teal rain cover tightly over an orange tent. Secure pegs and taut ropes are visible. Bedding remains dry inside the tent. A light rain shower falls in the woodland clearing.","focus":"keeping rain away from the bedding"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-02","title":"Reading a trail map","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Reading a map’s markings helps hikers choose a route.","Marked paths show possible ways to reach the campsite.","Landmarks help the hikers check where they are.","These clues help the group work out which path to follow.","A folded map fits neatly into a jacket pocket."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on using map markings to choose a route. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using map markings to choose a route. The spare sentence explains how to carry the map, rather than how to read its route clues.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze.","focus":"using map markings to choose a route"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-03","title":"Getting ready to write","image":"assets/illustrations/classroom-writing.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Preparing her desk helps Lina get ready to write.","Her open notebook gives her room for a sentence.","Her pencil rests where she can easily reach it.","With her materials ready, Lina can begin her writing.","Lina plans a surprising ending for her story."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on preparing a writing space. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on preparing a writing space. Planning the story’s ending concerns its content, rather than preparing the writing space.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl in a mustard cardigan, sits at a clear classroom desk. Her open notebook and pencil are prominent as she begins writing. A closed schoolbag is beside the desk. Unreadable small pencil marks only, no printed words.","focus":"preparing a writing space"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-04","title":"Fitting a bicycle helmet","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Checking a helmet’s fit helps it stay in the right position.","The helmet sits low and level on the rider’s head.","Fastened straps stop it from shifting easily.","These checks help the helmet fit securely before the ride.","Reflectors help drivers notice a bicycle in dim light."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on making sure a helmet fits properly. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on making sure a helmet fits properly. Reflectors are also safety equipment, but they do not explain how a helmet should fit.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety.","focus":"making sure a helmet fits properly"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-05","title":"Choosing a kite-flying space","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Choosing a clear flying area gives a kite enough space.","An open field gives the string room to stretch.","Space away from trees keeps it clear of branches.","A suitable place gives the kite room to rise and move.","A long tail helps a kite stay steady in the wind."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on choosing a clear place to fly a kite. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on choosing a clear place to fly a kite. The tail helps the kite balance. The paragraph is about choosing a clear flying area.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space.","focus":"choosing a clear place to fly a kite"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-06","title":"Preparing a picnic spot","image":"assets/illustrations/park-picnic.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Preparing a picnic spot makes an outdoor meal comfortable.","A dry patch of grass is a good place for the blanket.","An open basket puts the lunch within easy reach.","With the spot ready, the friends can sit down to eat.","One friend tells a funny story during lunch."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on getting a comfortable place ready for lunch. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on getting a comfortable place ready for lunch. Telling a story is part of enjoying lunch, rather than preparing the picnic spot.","alt":"Two friends, a girl with light-brown skin and glasses and a boy with black hair, sit on a clearly spread yellow picnic blanket in a green park. A woven picnic basket sits between their bags. Lunch containers and apple slices are on the blanket. A level grassy patch beside a broad park path.","focus":"getting a comfortable place ready for lunch"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-07","title":"Preparing to sail","image":"assets/illustrations/sailing-ropes.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Checking equipment is part of preparing for a sailing lesson.","The instructor checks that the ropes are in place.","The children check that their life jackets fit securely.","These equipment checks help the group begin safely.","The instructor demonstrates how to steer around a buoy."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on checking equipment before the sailing lesson. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on checking equipment before the sailing lesson. Steering around a buoy is something to practise during sailing, rather than an equipment check.","alt":"An adult male sailing instructor checks neatly coiled ropes on a small training sailboat beside a sheltered marina dock. Two children in properly fastened life jackets watch attentively. The boat has a prominent pale sail, a safe simple hull and tidy rigging. Calm harbour water and distant colourful boats.","focus":"checking equipment before the sailing lesson"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-08","title":"A safe first dive","image":"assets/illustrations/shallow-dive.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Safe conditions help beginners practise their diving skills.","An instructor stays close enough to guide the learners.","Their checked diving equipment provides the air they need.","Guidance and suitable equipment help the lesson begin safely.","The learners compare the colours of two passing fish."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on safe conditions for a beginner diving lesson. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on safe conditions for a beginner diving lesson. Comparing fish is an observation activity. It does not explain the lesson’s safety arrangements.","alt":"An adult scuba instructor supervises two children during a beginner lesson in clear shallow water above a sandy seabed. All have coherent fitted scuba gear, masks, regulators and air tanks. Sunlight reaches the visible bottom. Calm close supervision, no animals touched and no deep-water danger.","focus":"safe conditions for a beginner diving lesson"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-09","title":"Removing garden weeds","image":"assets/illustrations/garden-helpers.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Removing weeds reduces crowding around young vegetables.","Sofia pulls the unwanted plants out of the soil.","Her bucket keeps the pulled weeds out of the garden bed.","This weeding leaves more space around the vegetables.","The vegetables will be washed before they are cooked."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on giving vegetable plants room by removing weeds. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on giving vegetable plants room by removing weeds. Preparing vegetables for a meal is a different task. It does not explain removing weeds from the bed.","alt":"Sofia, a Latina girl with a dark ponytail, kneels beside a raised vegetable bed. She gently pulls a weed and drops it into a small blue bucket beside her. Neat rows of young vegetables are visible. A bee visits a yellow flower at the edge of the bed, clearly separate from Sofia's hands.","focus":"giving vegetable plants room by removing weeds"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-10","title":"Mixing cake batter","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Careful mixing brings cake ingredients together in a bowl.","A steady bowl keeps the ingredients together.","Gentle stirring combines them without splashing them out.","The mixed batter is then ready for the next step.","The oven is set to the temperature the recipe needs."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on bringing ingredients together in the mixing bowl. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on bringing ingredients together in the mixing bowl. Setting the oven concerns baking, rather than combining ingredients in the mixing bowl.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin.","focus":"bringing ingredients together in the mixing bowl"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-11","title":"Preparing a science workspace","image":"assets/illustrations/science-tray.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A prepared workspace helps keep a science experiment tidy.","A tray beneath the cup catches stray drips.","A clear area gives the children room for their equipment.","These preparations keep the work area easier to use.","The children write down the changes they observe."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on keeping the experiment’s workspace clear and tidy. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on keeping the experiment’s workspace clear and tidy. Writing observations records the experiment’s results. It does not describe preparing the workspace.","alt":"Ruby, a fair-skinned girl with auburn hair, and Min, an East Asian boy with glasses, share a classroom science table. Wearing safety goggles, they pour water between clear cups above a shallow tray. A few drops land in the tray, keeping the surrounding table dry. Friendly teacher in the background.","focus":"keeping the experiment’s workspace clear and tidy"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-12","title":"Dressing for snow","image":"assets/illustrations/snow-ready.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Warm clothing helps children prepare for a snowy day.","Gloves protect their fingers from the cold snow.","Winter coats help keep their bodies warm outside.","Dressing for the weather makes outdoor play more comfortable.","The children use a sled to travel down a gentle hill."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on choosing clothes that keep the body warm. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on choosing clothes that keep the body warm. The sled is used for a snowy activity. The paragraph explains clothing that keeps the body warm.","alt":"Kwame, a Black boy in a blue winter coat, carries a small red sled along a snowy path toward a gentle hill. His friend wears a purple coat. Both children have warm hats, thick gloves and snow boots; the gloves and sled are clearly visible. Sunny winter park.","focus":"choosing clothes that keep the body warm"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-13","title":"Shaping a sandcastle","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Simple tools help form a sandcastle’s main shapes.","A bucket can shape damp sand into towers.","Small scoops move sand into the gaps between the walls.","Using these tools helps the castle take shape.","Shells pressed into the walls make a colourful pattern."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on using tools to form the castle’s main shapes. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using tools to form the castle’s main shapes. The shells add decoration to existing walls, rather than forming the castle’s main sand shapes.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby.","focus":"using tools to form the castle’s main shapes"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-14","title":"Waiting safely at a station","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Passengers follow safety rules while waiting on a platform.","The safety line keeps waiting passengers back from the edge.","Clear walkways give other passengers room to pass.","These habits help people wait safely for their train.","A ticket shows which train service a passenger has booked."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on waiting safely on the platform. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on waiting safely on the platform. The ticket identifies a service. The paragraph explains safe behaviour while waiting on the platform.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print.","focus":"waiting safely on the platform"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-15","title":"Fresh water for a dog","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Fresh drinking water should be easy for a dog to reach.","A clean bowl keeps the water in one place.","An easy-to-reach spot lets the dog drink when it needs to.","Checking the water regularly helps meet this need.","Brushing the dog’s coat removes loose fur."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on making fresh drinking water available to a dog. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on making fresh drinking water available to a dog. Brushing is another kind of dog care, but it does not make drinking water available.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them.","focus":"making fresh drinking water available to a dog"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-16","title":"Passing as a team","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Passing is one way football players share the ball.","Looking up helps a player notice a ready teammate.","A controlled kick sends the ball towards that teammate.","Good passes give more players a part in the game.","A player practises aiming shots at the goal."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on moving the ball between football teammates. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on moving the ball between football teammates. Shooting aims the ball at the goal. This paragraph explains passing it to another player.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline.","focus":"moving the ball between football teammates"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-17","title":"Choosing a library book","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Clues in a book help a reader decide whether it is a good fit.","The cover offers clues about what the story may contain.","A few pages show the reader how the story is written.","Looking at these clues helps the reader make a choice.","A plastic cover protects the book while it is on loan."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on using clues from a book to decide whether to read it. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using clues from a book to decide whether to read it. The plastic cover protects the book. It does not offer clues to help the reader choose a story.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages.","focus":"using clues from a book to decide whether to read it"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-18","title":"Building safely with an adult","image":"assets/illustrations/measuring-board.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Adult guidance helps children work safely on a treehouse.","An adult checks measurements before any boards are cut.","The adult handles tools that are unsuitable for children.","Following this guidance lets the children learn safely.","Paint colours can help a treehouse blend with nearby leaves."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on working safely with adult guidance. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on working safely with adult guidance. Choosing colours changes how the treehouse looks. It does not explain safe working arrangements.","alt":"An adult builder steadies a sturdy long wooden board flat on a low workbench while two children carefully measure it with a tape measure. All wear safety glasses. A small partly built treehouse appears safely at ground level behind them. No power tools in use, no readable measurements.","focus":"working safely with adult guidance"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-19","title":"A strong model bridge","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A model bridge needs a structure that supports its crossing.","Supports hold up the centre of the bridge.","Joined craft sticks form the sides of the crossing.","These parts work together to hold the model firmly.","The bridge is painted to match a nearby model village."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on building the parts that support a model bridge. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on building the parts that support a model bridge. Matching paint colours concerns appearance, rather than the parts supporting the crossing.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby.","focus":"building the parts that support a model bridge"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-20","title":"Sharing mixing jobs","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Sharing mixing tasks helps kitchen helpers work together.","One helper steadies the bowl during mixing.","Another helper stirs the ingredients with a spoon.","Giving each person a job makes the mixing easier to share.","The recipe combines flour, eggs and milk in one mixture."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on sharing the jobs during mixing. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on sharing the jobs during mixing. The ingredients describe what is being mixed. The paragraph explains who does each mixing job.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin.","focus":"sharing the jobs during mixing"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-21","title":"Watching wildlife from a distance","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Binoculars let hikers examine wildlife from a distance.","The lenses make distant shapes appear larger.","The hikers can stay on the path while watching.","This tool helps them see closely without moving nearer.","A soft case protects the binoculars inside a backpack."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on using binoculars to see distant wildlife. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using binoculars to see distant wildlife. The case protects the binoculars during storage. It does not explain using them to observe from a distance.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze.","focus":"using binoculars to see distant wildlife"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-22","title":"Making a snowman’s base","image":"assets/illustrations/snowman.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A snowman needs a broad base to support its upper parts.","Rolling a snowball across fresh snow adds more snow to it.","A broad base gives the upper snowballs a place to rest.","A carefully built base helps support the finished snowman.","A scarf gives the snowman a cheerful winter look."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on forming a base that can support a snowman. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on forming a base that can support a snowman. The scarf decorates the snowman. It does not help build its supporting base.","alt":"Two children in warm coats, gloves and boots roll a very large snowball across level snow to build a snowman. A smaller ball waits nearby, with a carrot and two plain pebbles in a basket. The giant lower ball is clearly much larger than their smaller snowballs. Joyful sunny winter park.","focus":"forming a base that can support a snowman"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-23","title":"Talking about a shared story","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Talking about a shared story helps friends understand it.","Reading the same page gives them something to discuss.","Talking about a picture helps them notice new details.","Sharing their ideas can make the story easier to understand.","They use a bookmark to save the page for tomorrow."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on understanding a story by discussing it together. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on understanding a story by discussing it together. The bookmark saves their place for later. It does not describe understanding the story through discussion.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages.","focus":"understanding a story by discussing it together"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-24","title":"Magnifying a leaf","image":"assets/illustrations/leaf-study.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A magnifying glass makes small leaf details easier to see.","Its lens enlarges the view of the leaf’s tiny lines.","The leaf can be viewed without changing its actual size.","This tool reveals details that are hard to see unaided.","Pressing a leaf between dry pages helps preserve it."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on how a magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on how a magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf. Pressing preserves the leaf, rather than enlarging the details seen through a lens.","alt":"Two children study a green leaf at a classroom light table. One child holds a magnifying glass over the leaf's clearly visible veins; the other holds a transparent plastic sheet partly across the leaf so it remains visible through the clear material. Careful natural hand poses, a simple uncluttered science table.","focus":"how a magnifying glass changes the view of a leaf"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-25","title":"Checking a robot’s connection","image":"assets/illustrations/robot-partners.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Checking a connection can help solve a robot’s power problem.","A loose plug may stop power from reaching part of the robot.","A glowing indicator gives clues about the connection.","These checks help the builders trace the power problem.","Different wheel sizes change how the robot moves."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on checking an electrical connection in a robot. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on checking an electrical connection in a robot. Wheel sizes affect movement. The paragraph focuses on tracing an electrical connection problem.","alt":"Nia, a Black girl with braided hair, and Arjun, a South Asian boy with glasses, check their small wheeled classroom robot on a table. Arjun reconnects a loose low-voltage plug while Nia watches a green indicator light glow. A delighted teacher stands behind. No exposed mains wiring, no labels.","focus":"checking an electrical connection in a robot"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-26","title":"Comparing glider landings","image":"assets/illustrations/paper-gliders.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Recording glider landings gives the flyers results to compare.","Maya’s glider lands on a clear patch of grass.","Ben’s glider drifts sideways into a bush.","Comparing the landings helps the flyers plan another test.","A fold down the middle gives each glider two wings."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on comparing where gliders land in a flight test. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on comparing where gliders land in a flight test. The fold describes the gliders’ construction. It does not record or compare their flight results.","alt":"Ben, a red-haired boy, and Maya, a girl with dark braids, test two plain paper gliders on an open grassy lawn. One glider has drifted gently into a low bush while the other rests in Maya's hand. Ben walks toward the bush to retrieve the glider. A coherent outdoor scene with both gliders easy to see.","focus":"comparing where gliders land in a flight test"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-27","title":"Spotting a ready basketball teammate","image":"assets/illustrations/basketball-pass.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A basketball passer looks for signs of a ready teammate.","A player facing the ball can watch it approach.","Empty raised hands show that the teammate can try to catch it.","These clues help the passer choose a sensible moment.","A shooter bends their knees before aiming at the hoop."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on noticing that a teammate is ready to catch a pass. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on noticing that a teammate is ready to catch a pass. Aiming at the hoop prepares a shot, rather than showing readiness to receive a teammate’s pass.","alt":"Two children practise a basketball chest pass on an outdoor court. One girl stands ready with bent knees and open hands while a boy gently passes the basketball toward her. A female coach supervises nearby. Realistic readable body positions, one ball and safe spacing.","focus":"noticing that a teammate is ready to catch a pass"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-28","title":"Brushing a pony safely","image":"assets/illustrations/pony-care.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Gentle, supervised brushing helps clean a pony’s coat.","A suitable brush lifts dust from the coat.","An instructor helps the children stand in a safe place.","With guidance, they can brush without upsetting the pony.","The pony follows a regular feeding routine each day."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on cleaning a pony’s coat through gentle, supervised brushing. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on cleaning a pony’s coat through gentle, supervised brushing. A feeding routine is another part of pony care, but it does not explain gentle, supervised brushing.","alt":"Priya, a South Asian girl wearing a fitted riding helmet and closed riding boots, gently brushes a calm brown pony's bare back in a stable aisle. An adult instructor holds the pony's lead rope. A saddle waits separately on a stand, clearly not yet on the pony. Warm calm light.","focus":"cleaning a pony’s coat through gentle, supervised brushing"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-29","title":"Studying a museum display","image":"assets/illustrations/museum-fossil.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["Observation and a guide’s explanations help visitors learn.","Looking closely reveals details in the fossil display.","The guide explains ideas that are not clear from looking alone.","Using both sources helps visitors understand the display.","A padded storage box protects the fossil during travel."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on using observation and a guide to understand a display. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using observation and a guide to understand a display. The storage box protects the fossil. It does not explain how visitors study the display.","alt":"An adult museum guide shows a large spiral fossil in a low glass display case to a small group of fascinated children. One child uses a manual wheelchair and has a clear view beside the other visitors. A skeleton exhibit is softly visible behind them. No labels or readable signage.","focus":"using observation and a guide to understand a display"},{"id":"paragraph-AA-30","title":"Discussing a space model","image":"assets/illustrations/space-club.webp","question":"Build a paragraph that stays on the topic. Leave one sentence out.","sentences":["A shared space model helps children explain ideas to each other.","One display gives everyone the same model to examine.","Taking turns pointing lets different children explain ideas.","The shared model supports their questions and discussion.","Clear varnish protects the model’s painted surface."],"orders":[[0,1,2,3],[0,2,1,3]],"hint":"Focus on using a shared model to explain ideas to one another. Keep the details that explain this main idea.","why":"The paragraph focuses on using a shared model to explain ideas to one another. The varnish protects the model. It does not explain using the model for group discussion.","alt":"A diverse group of three children in an after-school space club gathers around a tabletop solar-system model. They point to small colourful planets attached to thin supports around a large central sun. Warm classroom, thoughtful curious expressions, no printed labels or floating text.","focus":"using a shared model to explain ideas to one another"}]},"meaning":{"A":[{"id":"meaning-A-01","title":"Careful builders","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"The model was {fragile}, so Lina carried it with both hands.","question":"What does “fragile” mean here?","options":["easily broken","very heavy","already finished"],"answer":"easily broken","hint":"Notice why Lina needs to carry the model carefully.","why":"“Fragile” means easily broken or damaged.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"meaning-A-02","title":"A clear route","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The map showed the {route} to the campsite.","question":"What does “route” mean here?","options":["the way to a place","a place to sleep","the time to leave"],"answer":"the way to a place","hint":"The hikers follow the line to reach the campsite.","why":"“Route” means the way or path taken to reach a place.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"meaning-A-03","title":"A shallow dive","image":"assets/illustrations/shallow-dive.webp","passage":"The water was {shallow}, so the instructor stayed close to the surface.","question":"What does “shallow” mean here?","options":["not deep","not clear","not warm"],"answer":"not deep","hint":"Compare the bottom with the surface.","why":"“Shallow” means not deep.","alt":"An adult scuba instructor supervises two children during a beginner lesson in clear shallow water above a sandy seabed. All have coherent fitted scuba gear, masks, regulators and air tanks. Sunlight reaches the visible bottom. Calm close supervision, no animals touched and no deep-water danger."},{"id":"meaning-A-04","title":"A wet towel","image":"assets/illustrations/wet-towel.webp","passage":"The towel was {damp}, so Maya spread it out to dry.","question":"What does “damp” mean here?","options":["a little wet","completely dry","covered in mud"],"answer":"a little wet","hint":"The towel needs drying but is only slightly wet.","why":"“Damp” means slightly wet.","alt":"A child at a sunny woodland campsite lifts a visibly wet towel from a washing bowl. Water drips from the towel onto the grass as a second child points to a nearby drying line. A tent and a small wash station in the background, one clear everyday action."},{"id":"meaning-A-05","title":"Stirring slowly","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"Mila stirred {gently} so the batter stayed in the bowl.","question":"What does “gently” mean here?","options":["with care and little force","with a loud noise","with great speed"],"answer":"with care and little force","hint":"Notice how Mila prevents the batter from splashing.","why":"“Gently” means carefully, using little force.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"meaning-A-06","title":"A strong board","image":"assets/illustrations/measuring-board.webp","passage":"The builder chose a {sturdy} board that would not bend easily.","question":"What does “sturdy” mean here?","options":["strong and firm","thin and delicate","brightly coloured"],"answer":"strong and firm","hint":"The board must hold weight.","why":"“Sturdy” means strong, firm and unlikely to give way.","alt":"An adult builder steadies a sturdy long wooden board flat on a low workbench while two children carefully measure it with a tape measure. All wear safety glasses. A small partly built treehouse appears safely at ground level behind them. No power tools in use, no readable measurements."},{"id":"meaning-A-07","title":"A giant snowball","image":"assets/illustrations/snowman.webp","passage":"The snowball became {enormous} as Poppy rolled it.","question":"What does “enormous” mean here?","options":["very large","very smooth","very cold"],"answer":"very large","hint":"Look at how the snowball changes in size.","why":"“Enormous” means very large.","alt":"Two children in warm coats, gloves and boots roll a very large snowball across level snow to build a snowman. A smaller ball waits nearby, with a carrot and two plain pebbles in a basket. The giant lower ball is clearly much larger than their smaller snowballs. Joyful sunny winter park."},{"id":"meaning-A-08","title":"Before a new trick","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Finn {hesitated} before trying the new ramp.","question":"What does “hesitated” mean here?","options":["paused before acting","hurried without looking","forgot what had happened"],"answer":"paused before acting","hint":"Finn stops and thinks before beginning.","why":"“Hesitated” means paused because of uncertainty or thought.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"meaning-A-09","title":"Beach helpers","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"The friends {gathered} litter into one bag.","question":"What does “gathered” mean here?","options":["collected together","spread farther apart","covered with sand"],"answer":"collected together","hint":"The scattered items end up together in one bag.","why":"“Gathered” means collected or brought together.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."},{"id":"meaning-A-10","title":"A jacket strap","image":"assets/illustrations/life-jacket-check.webp","passage":"The instructor needed to {adjust} the loose strap.","question":"What does “adjust” mean here?","options":["change a little to make it fit","remove and throw away","cover so it cannot be seen"],"answer":"change a little to make it fit","hint":"The jacket stays on while the fit changes.","why":"“Adjust” means change something slightly to make it fit or work better.","alt":"An adult female sailing instructor in a navy jacket gently tightens a loose life-jacket strap on a child before boarding a small boat. Show the fitted life jacket and closed buckle prominently. Another child waits wearing a properly fastened life jacket. Calm marina dock, safely away from the edge."},{"id":"meaning-A-11","title":"A long hike","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"After the long climb, the hikers were {exhausted}.","question":"What does “exhausted” mean here?","options":["very tired","very lost","very excited"],"answer":"very tired","hint":"The long climb leaves the hikers needing rest.","why":"“Exhausted” means very tired.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"meaning-A-12","title":"A secure tent","image":"assets/illustrations/rain-cover.webp","passage":"The pegs kept the tent {secure} in the wind.","question":"What does “secure” mean here?","options":["firmly held in place","completely empty","easy to carry"],"answer":"firmly held in place","hint":"The wind cannot pull the pegs free.","why":"“Secure” means firmly fixed or safely held in place.","alt":"Maya, a brown-skinned girl with two braids, and Ben, a fair-skinned boy with curly red hair, pull a waterproof teal rain cover tightly over an orange tent. Secure pegs and taut ropes are visible. Bedding remains dry inside the tent. A light rain shower falls in the woodland clearing."},{"id":"meaning-A-13","title":"A closer look","image":"assets/illustrations/leaf-study.webp","passage":"Min was {curious} about the tiny lines in the leaf.","question":"What does “curious” mean here?","options":["wanting to find out more","wanting to stop working","feeling sure of every answer"],"answer":"wanting to find out more","hint":"Min wants to discover something.","why":"“Curious” means wanting to learn or find out more.","alt":"Two children study a green leaf at a classroom light table. One child holds a magnifying glass over the leaf's clearly visible veins; the other holds a transparent plastic sheet partly across the leaf so it remains visible through the clear material. Careful natural hand poses, a simple uncluttered science table."},{"id":"meaning-A-14","title":"Waiting for a turn","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Asha was {patient} while Finn finished his turn.","question":"What does “patient” mean here?","options":["able to wait calmly","ready to leave quickly","worried about getting lost"],"answer":"able to wait calmly","hint":"Asha waits without rushing her friend.","why":"“Patient” means able to wait calmly without becoming upset.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"meaning-A-15","title":"A clear sheet","image":"assets/illustrations/leaf-study.webp","passage":"The {transparent} sheet let the children see the leaf below.","question":"What does “transparent” mean here?","options":["clear enough to see through","too thick to lift","able to change colour"],"answer":"clear enough to see through","hint":"The children can see through the new sheet.","why":"“Transparent” means allowing you to see through it.","alt":"Two children study a green leaf at a classroom light table. One child holds a magnifying glass over the leaf's clearly visible veins; the other holds a transparent plastic sheet partly across the leaf so it remains visible through the clear material. Careful natural hand poses, a simple uncluttered science table."},{"id":"meaning-A-16","title":"A rough track","image":"assets/illustrations/jeep-trail.webp","passage":"The jeep moved slowly along the {uneven} track.","question":"What does “uneven” mean here?","options":["not smooth or level","not long enough","not marked on a map"],"answer":"not smooth or level","hint":"Look for the dips and bumps.","why":"“Uneven” means not smooth, flat or level.","alt":"A family pauses in a stationary open-top safari jeep on a rough stony woodland track. The child in the back seat touches the smooth padded seat beside them; all occupants wear correctly fastened seat belts. An adult driver holds a map at the meeting point. No traffic danger, no readable plate or signs."},{"id":"meaning-A-17","title":"Checking a ticket","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"The conductor would {inspect} each ticket before the trip.","question":"What does “inspect” mean here?","options":["look at carefully","give away freely","fold into a shape"],"answer":"look at carefully","hint":"The conductor checks the ticket’s details.","why":"“Inspect” means examine or look at carefully.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"meaning-A-18","title":"A passing train","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"The last carriage {vanished} around the bend.","question":"What does “vanished” mean here?","options":["disappeared from view","stopped without moving","became louder"],"answer":"disappeared from view","hint":"The carriage can no longer be seen.","why":"“Vanished” means disappeared from sight.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"meaning-A-19","title":"Enough batter","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"The bowl held {sufficient} batter for the small cake.","question":"What does “sufficient” mean here?","options":["enough for the purpose","more than could ever fit","too little to use"],"answer":"enough for the purpose","hint":"The baker does not need to make any more.","why":"“Sufficient” means enough for what is needed.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"meaning-A-20","title":"Robot success","image":"assets/illustrations/robot-partners.webp","passage":"Nia was {delighted} when the robot’s light came on.","question":"What does “delighted” mean here?","options":["very pleased","very puzzled","very sleepy"],"answer":"very pleased","hint":"Nia’s wide smile is a clue.","why":"“Delighted” means very pleased or happy.","alt":"Nia, a Black girl with braided hair, and Arjun, a South Asian boy with glasses, check their small wheeled classroom robot on a table. Arjun reconnects a loose low-voltage plug while Nia watches a green indicator light glow. A delighted teacher stands behind. No exposed mains wiring, no labels."},{"id":"meaning-A-21","title":"A tight fit","image":"assets/illustrations/glider-box.webp","passage":"The glider would not fit in the {narrow} box.","question":"What does “narrow” mean here?","options":["not wide","not deep","not clean"],"answer":"not wide","hint":"Compare the wide wings with the box opening.","why":"“Narrow” means not wide.","alt":"At a classroom craft table a child tries to place a broad paper glider into a long narrow open cardboard box. The glider's wings visibly extend beyond both sides of the box, making the box clearly too narrow. A friend compares the wingspan and box opening. Do not bend, squash or damage the glider."},{"id":"meaning-A-22","title":"Out of the wind","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers rested in a {sheltered} spot behind a rock.","question":"What does “sheltered” mean here?","options":["protected from wind or weather","far away from everyone","difficult to reach"],"answer":"protected from wind or weather","hint":"The large rock blocks the wind.","why":"“Sheltered” means protected from wind, weather or other exposure.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"meaning-A-23","title":"Quick movement","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","passage":"The football rolled at a {rapid} pace.","question":"What does “rapid” mean here?","options":["fast","steady but slow","hard to predict"],"answer":"fast","hint":"The ball reaches the next player very quickly.","why":"“Rapid” means fast or happening quickly.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline."},{"id":"meaning-A-24","title":"A safer ride","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"A helmet helps {prevent} a head injury.","question":"What does “prevent” mean here?","options":["stop something from happening","describe something afterward","make something happen sooner"],"answer":"stop something from happening","hint":"The helmet is worn before a possible fall.","why":"“Prevent” means stop something from happening.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"meaning-A-25","title":"A smooth seat","image":"assets/illustrations/jeep-trail.webp","passage":"The jeep’s seat felt {smooth} under Lina’s hand.","question":"What does “smooth” mean here?","options":["even and not rough","soft and very deep","bright and very shiny"],"answer":"even and not rough","hint":"The clue is the absence of rough bumps.","why":"“Smooth” means even and free from rough bumps.","alt":"A family pauses in a stationary open-top safari jeep on a rough stony woodland track. The child in the back seat touches the smooth padded seat beside them; all occupants wear correctly fastened seat belts. An adult driver holds a map at the meeting point. No traffic danger, no readable plate or signs."},{"id":"meaning-A-26","title":"Letting go","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"Jamal would {release} a little more kite string.","question":"What does “release” mean here?","options":["let go or let out","pull back tightly","tie into a knot"],"answer":"let go or let out","hint":"Jamal loosens his grip instead of pulling back.","why":"“Release” means let go or allow something to come out.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"meaning-A-27","title":"Filling the bowl","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","passage":"The bowl was {empty} before the water was added.","question":"What does “empty” mean here?","options":["holding nothing","holding too much","holding something dirty"],"answer":"holding nothing","hint":"There is nothing inside the bowl.","why":"“Empty” means containing nothing.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them."},{"id":"meaning-A-28","title":"Staying upright","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"Sofia stayed {balanced} as she rode slowly.","question":"What does “balanced” mean here?","options":["steady without tipping","quick without stopping","quiet without speaking"],"answer":"steady without tipping","hint":"The rider does not tip to either side.","why":"“Balanced” means steady, with weight supported so something does not tip.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"meaning-A-29","title":"Rock-pool care","image":"assets/illustrations/rock-pools.webp","passage":"The children were {cautious} on the wet rocks.","question":"What does “cautious” mean here?","options":["careful about possible danger","certain nothing could go wrong","eager to hurry ahead"],"answer":"careful about possible danger","hint":"The wet rocks could be slippery.","why":"“Cautious” means careful to avoid possible danger.","alt":"Two children crouch beside shallow seawater pools between flat coastal rocks at low tide. They look closely at a tiny crab and shells without touching or disturbing them. An attentive adult guide is beside them. Non-slip shoes, stable rock surfaces and gentle daylight."},{"id":"meaning-A-30","title":"A quiet place","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"The reading corner was {peaceful}.","question":"What does “peaceful” mean here?","options":["calm and quiet","busy and crowded","new and unfamiliar"],"answer":"calm and quiet","hint":"Look for the lack of noise and interruption.","why":"“Peaceful” means calm and quiet.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."}],"AA":[{"id":"meaning-AA-01","title":"Careful builders","image":"assets/illustrations/model-bridge.webp","passage":"The thin craft sticks could snap if the model fell. Lina knew it was {fragile}, so she carried it with both hands.","question":"What does “fragile” mean here?","options":["easily broken","very heavy","already finished"],"answer":"easily broken","hint":"Notice why Lina needs to carry the model carefully.","why":"“Fragile” means easily broken or damaged.","alt":"Lina, an East Asian girl with a yellow top, and Andre, a Black boy in a blue jumper, carefully align craft sticks to make a small model bridge on their classroom table. Their completed bridge spans two supports. A ruler, child-safe glue and a few spare sticks lie neatly nearby."},{"id":"meaning-AA-02","title":"A clear route","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers traced a line along the path on their map. It showed the {route} they would follow to the campsite.","question":"What does “route” mean here?","options":["the way to a place","a place to sleep","the time to leave"],"answer":"the way to a place","hint":"The hikers follow the line to reach the campsite.","why":"“Route” means the way or path taken to reach a place.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"meaning-AA-03","title":"A shallow dive","image":"assets/illustrations/shallow-dive.webp","passage":"The lesson took place in {shallow} water, with the sandy bottom only a short distance below the surface.","question":"What does “shallow” mean here?","options":["not deep","not clear","not warm"],"answer":"not deep","hint":"Compare the bottom with the surface.","why":"“Shallow” means not deep.","alt":"An adult scuba instructor supervises two children during a beginner lesson in clear shallow water above a sandy seabed. All have coherent fitted scuba gear, masks, regulators and air tanks. Sunlight reaches the visible bottom. Calm close supervision, no animals touched and no deep-water danger."},{"id":"meaning-AA-04","title":"A wet towel","image":"assets/illustrations/wet-towel.webp","passage":"The towel felt slightly wet after the picnic. Because it was still {damp}, Maya spread it out in the air.","question":"What does “damp” mean here?","options":["a little wet","completely dry","covered in mud"],"answer":"a little wet","hint":"The towel needs drying but is only slightly wet.","why":"“Damp” means slightly wet.","alt":"A child at a sunny woodland campsite lifts a visibly wet towel from a washing bowl. Water drips from the towel onto the grass as a second child points to a nearby drying line. A tent and a small wash station in the background, one clear everyday action."},{"id":"meaning-AA-05","title":"Stirring slowly","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"The bowl was nearly full. Mila moved the spoon slowly and {gently}, keeping the batter away from the edge.","question":"What does “gently” mean here?","options":["with care and little force","with a loud noise","with great speed"],"answer":"with care and little force","hint":"Notice how Mila prevents the batter from splashing.","why":"“Gently” means carefully, using little force.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"meaning-AA-06","title":"A strong board","image":"assets/illustrations/measuring-board.webp","passage":"The builder needed a board that could hold weight without bending. A {sturdy} piece was the best choice.","question":"What does “sturdy” mean here?","options":["strong and firm","thin and delicate","brightly coloured"],"answer":"strong and firm","hint":"The board must hold weight.","why":"“Sturdy” means strong, firm and unlikely to give way.","alt":"An adult builder steadies a sturdy long wooden board flat on a low workbench while two children carefully measure it with a tape measure. All wear safety glasses. A small partly built treehouse appears safely at ground level behind them. No power tools in use, no readable measurements."},{"id":"meaning-AA-07","title":"A giant snowball","image":"assets/illustrations/snowman.webp","passage":"Each turn collected more snow until the snowball was {enormous}, much larger than it had been at the start.","question":"What does “enormous” mean here?","options":["very large","very smooth","very cold"],"answer":"very large","hint":"Look at how the snowball changes in size.","why":"“Enormous” means very large.","alt":"Two children in warm coats, gloves and boots roll a very large snowball across level snow to build a snowman. A smaller ball waits nearby, with a carrot and two plain pebbles in a basket. The giant lower ball is clearly much larger than their smaller snowballs. Joyful sunny winter park."},{"id":"meaning-AA-08","title":"Before a new trick","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Finn stopped at the top of the small ramp and thought for a moment. He {hesitated} before beginning the unfamiliar move.","question":"What does “hesitated” mean here?","options":["paused before acting","hurried without looking","forgot what had happened"],"answer":"paused before acting","hint":"Finn stops and thinks before beginning.","why":"“Hesitated” means paused because of uncertainty or thought.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"meaning-AA-09","title":"Beach helpers","image":"assets/illustrations/sandcastle-team.webp","passage":"The friends walked along the sand, collecting the scattered wrappers. They {gathered} the litter into one bag.","question":"What does “gathered” mean here?","options":["collected together","spread farther apart","covered with sand"],"answer":"collected together","hint":"The scattered items end up together in one bag.","why":"“Gathered” means collected or brought together.","alt":"Mei, an East Asian girl with straight black hair and a sun hat, carries two small buckets full of damp sand toward a sandcastle. Her friend shapes a castle wall nearby. Gentle sea in the background, sunny beach, sensible sun protection and an adult supervising from nearby."},{"id":"meaning-AA-10","title":"A jacket strap","image":"assets/illustrations/life-jacket-check.webp","passage":"The life jacket was already on, but one strap hung loosely. The instructor needed to {adjust} it for a better fit.","question":"What does “adjust” mean here?","options":["change a little to make it fit","remove and throw away","cover so it cannot be seen"],"answer":"change a little to make it fit","hint":"The jacket stays on while the fit changes.","why":"“Adjust” means change something slightly to make it fit or work better.","alt":"An adult female sailing instructor in a navy jacket gently tightens a loose life-jacket strap on a child before boarding a small boat. Show the fitted life jacket and closed buckle prominently. Another child waits wearing a properly fastened life jacket. Calm marina dock, safely away from the edge."},{"id":"meaning-AA-11","title":"A long hike","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"The hikers had climbed for a long time and needed to sit and rest. They felt {exhausted} when they reached the stopping place.","question":"What does “exhausted” mean here?","options":["very tired","very lost","very excited"],"answer":"very tired","hint":"The long climb leaves the hikers needing rest.","why":"“Exhausted” means very tired.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"meaning-AA-12","title":"A secure tent","image":"assets/illustrations/rain-cover.webp","passage":"Maya pushed each peg firmly into the ground so the wind could not pull it out. The tent was now {secure}.","question":"What does “secure” mean here?","options":["firmly held in place","completely empty","easy to carry"],"answer":"firmly held in place","hint":"The wind cannot pull the pegs free.","why":"“Secure” means firmly fixed or safely held in place.","alt":"Maya, a brown-skinned girl with two braids, and Ben, a fair-skinned boy with curly red hair, pull a waterproof teal rain cover tightly over an orange tent. Secure pegs and taut ropes are visible. Bedding remains dry inside the tent. A light rain shower falls in the woodland clearing."},{"id":"meaning-AA-13","title":"A closer look","image":"assets/illustrations/leaf-study.webp","passage":"Min wanted to discover why the leaf had so many tiny lines. Being {curious}, he looked through a magnifying glass.","question":"What does “curious” mean here?","options":["wanting to find out more","wanting to stop working","feeling sure of every answer"],"answer":"wanting to find out more","hint":"Min wants to discover something.","why":"“Curious” means wanting to learn or find out more.","alt":"Two children study a green leaf at a classroom light table. One child holds a magnifying glass over the leaf's clearly visible veins; the other holds a transparent plastic sheet partly across the leaf so it remains visible through the clear material. Careful natural hand poses, a simple uncluttered science table."},{"id":"meaning-AA-14","title":"Waiting for a turn","image":"assets/illustrations/skateboard-turn.webp","passage":"Asha waited calmly beside the ramp and did not rush Finn. She was {patient} while he finished practising.","question":"What does “patient” mean here?","options":["able to wait calmly","ready to leave quickly","worried about getting lost"],"answer":"able to wait calmly","hint":"Asha waits without rushing her friend.","why":"“Patient” means able to wait calmly without becoming upset.","alt":"Finn, a boy with freckles and brown curls, points to his skateboard beside a low beginners' ramp. His friend waits patiently behind the marked practice area as an adult instructor demonstrates a safe stance on another board. Every rider wears a correctly fastened helmet, wrist guards and knee pads."},{"id":"meaning-AA-15","title":"A clear sheet","image":"assets/illustrations/leaf-study.webp","passage":"The children replaced a cloudy sheet with a {transparent} one. They could now see the leaf’s tiny details through it.","question":"What does “transparent” mean here?","options":["clear enough to see through","too thick to lift","able to change colour"],"answer":"clear enough to see through","hint":"The children can see through the new sheet.","why":"“Transparent” means allowing you to see through it.","alt":"Two children study a green leaf at a classroom light table. One child holds a magnifying glass over the leaf's clearly visible veins; the other holds a transparent plastic sheet partly across the leaf so it remains visible through the clear material. Careful natural hand poses, a simple uncluttered science table."},{"id":"meaning-AA-16","title":"A rough track","image":"assets/illustrations/jeep-trail.webp","passage":"Small dips and bumps covered the track, so the driver slowed down on the {uneven} ground.","question":"What does “uneven” mean here?","options":["not smooth or level","not long enough","not marked on a map"],"answer":"not smooth or level","hint":"Look for the dips and bumps.","why":"“Uneven” means not smooth, flat or level.","alt":"A family pauses in a stationary open-top safari jeep on a rough stony woodland track. The child in the back seat touches the smooth padded seat beside them; all occupants wear correctly fastened seat belts. An adult driver holds a map at the meeting point. No traffic danger, no readable plate or signs."},{"id":"meaning-AA-17","title":"Checking a ticket","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"The conductor looked closely at each ticket to check its details. It was important to {inspect} every one before departure.","question":"What does “inspect” mean here?","options":["look at carefully","give away freely","fold into a shape"],"answer":"look at carefully","hint":"The conductor checks the ticket’s details.","why":"“Inspect” means examine or look at carefully.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"meaning-AA-18","title":"A passing train","image":"assets/illustrations/station-visit.webp","passage":"As the train travelled around the bend, its last carriage {vanished} behind the trees and could no longer be seen.","question":"What does “vanished” mean here?","options":["disappeared from view","stopped without moving","became louder"],"answer":"disappeared from view","hint":"The carriage can no longer be seen.","why":"“Vanished” means disappeared from sight.","alt":"A family waits together well behind the safety line on a railway platform. An adult conductor checks a child's plain ticket in the foreground while a bright passenger train approaches around a distant curve. Clear safe platform edge and coherent rails. No readable signs, numbers or ticket print."},{"id":"meaning-AA-19","title":"Enough batter","image":"assets/illustrations/baking-together.webp","passage":"The baker checked the amount in the bowl. There was {sufficient} batter to fill the small cake tin without making more.","question":"What does “sufficient” mean here?","options":["enough for the purpose","more than could ever fit","too little to use"],"answer":"enough for the purpose","hint":"The baker does not need to make any more.","why":"“Sufficient” means enough for what is needed.","alt":"Mila, a girl with short dark curls, wears a clean yellow apron and gently stirs cake batter with a wooden spoon. An adult baker with brown skin and a teal apron steadies the bowl at a child-height kitchen counter. Another child waits with a small jug. The large bowl holds enough batter for a nearby empty cake tin."},{"id":"meaning-AA-20","title":"Robot success","image":"assets/illustrations/robot-partners.webp","passage":"After carefully fixing the loose plug, Nia saw the robot’s green light glow. She smiled widely because she was {delighted}.","question":"What does “delighted” mean here?","options":["very pleased","very puzzled","very sleepy"],"answer":"very pleased","hint":"Nia’s wide smile is a clue.","why":"“Delighted” means very pleased or happy.","alt":"Nia, a Black girl with braided hair, and Arjun, a South Asian boy with glasses, check their small wheeled classroom robot on a table. Arjun reconnects a loose low-voltage plug while Nia watches a green indicator light glow. A delighted teacher stands behind. No exposed mains wiring, no labels."},{"id":"meaning-AA-21","title":"A tight fit","image":"assets/illustrations/glider-box.webp","passage":"The glider’s broad wings reached past both sides of the {narrow} box. The opening did not have much width.","question":"What does “narrow” mean here?","options":["not wide","not deep","not clean"],"answer":"not wide","hint":"Compare the wide wings with the box opening.","why":"“Narrow” means not wide.","alt":"At a classroom craft table a child tries to place a broad paper glider into a long narrow open cardboard box. The glider's wings visibly extend beyond both sides of the box, making the box clearly too narrow. A friend compares the wingspan and box opening. Do not bend, squash or damage the glider."},{"id":"meaning-AA-22","title":"Out of the wind","image":"assets/illustrations/trail-map.webp","passage":"A strong wind blew across the trail, but the large rock blocked it. The hikers rested in the {sheltered} spot behind it.","question":"What does “sheltered” mean here?","options":["protected from wind or weather","far away from everyone","difficult to reach"],"answer":"protected from wind or weather","hint":"The large rock blocks the wind.","why":"“Sheltered” means protected from wind, weather or other exposure.","alt":"Two young hikers rest on a fallen log in the shelter of a large rock beside a woodland trail. A girl with dark curly hair points along a clear route on an unfolded map while a blond boy holds binoculars. Water bottles and backpacks rest beside them. A small deer is far away on the hillside. The rock shelters them from the breeze."},{"id":"meaning-AA-23","title":"Quick movement","image":"assets/illustrations/football-team.webp","passage":"After the firm kick, the football travelled across the grass at a {rapid} pace and soon reached the next player.","question":"What does “rapid” mean here?","options":["fast","steady but slow","hard to predict"],"answer":"fast","hint":"The ball reaches the next player very quickly.","why":"“Rapid” means fast or happening quickly.","alt":"Coach Lee, an adult woman with short dark hair, watches children practise passing a football on a school field. One boy moves quickly to meet the ball while another child has just passed it. Clear football movement and safe spacing. A small group listens near the touchline."},{"id":"meaning-AA-24","title":"A safer ride","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"The instructor checked each helmet before the bicycle lesson. Wearing one helps {prevent} a head injury in a fall.","question":"What does “prevent” mean here?","options":["stop something from happening","describe something afterward","make something happen sooner"],"answer":"stop something from happening","hint":"The helmet is worn before a possible fall.","why":"“Prevent” means stop something from happening.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"meaning-AA-25","title":"A smooth seat","image":"assets/illustrations/jeep-trail.webp","passage":"Lina ran her hand across the jeep’s seat. The material felt {smooth}, with no rough bumps to catch her fingers.","question":"What does “smooth” mean here?","options":["even and not rough","soft and very deep","bright and very shiny"],"answer":"even and not rough","hint":"The clue is the absence of rough bumps.","why":"“Smooth” means even and free from rough bumps.","alt":"A family pauses in a stationary open-top safari jeep on a rough stony woodland track. The child in the back seat touches the smooth padded seat beside them; all occupants wear correctly fastened seat belts. An adult driver holds a map at the meeting point. No traffic danger, no readable plate or signs."},{"id":"meaning-AA-26","title":"Letting go","image":"assets/illustrations/kite-field.webp","passage":"As the kite climbed, Jamal loosened his grip to {release} a little more string from the spool.","question":"What does “release” mean here?","options":["let go or let out","pull back tightly","tie into a knot"],"answer":"let go or let out","hint":"Jamal loosens his grip instead of pulling back.","why":"“Release” means let go or allow something to come out.","alt":"Asha, a South Asian girl in a coral jacket, and Jamal, a Black boy in teal trousers, share a reel of string in a broad grassy field. Their colourful diamond kite is visibly airborne above them with its string connected to the reel. A small picnic basket and folded blanket sit off to one side. Breezy clouds and open space."},{"id":"meaning-AA-27","title":"Filling the bowl","image":"assets/illustrations/dog-water.webp","passage":"Sofia checked the dog’s bowl and found nothing inside. It was {empty}, so she began filling it with fresh water.","question":"What does “empty” mean here?","options":["holding nothing","holding too much","holding something dirty"],"answer":"holding nothing","hint":"There is nothing inside the bowl.","why":"“Empty” means containing nothing.","alt":"A child with a tan complexion pours fresh water from a small jug into a nearly full metal dog bowl on a shady garden path. A happy golden dog stands beside the bowl with its tongue out, ready for a drink. A coiled lead and closed garden gate appear behind them."},{"id":"meaning-AA-28","title":"Staying upright","image":"assets/illustrations/bicycle-practice.webp","passage":"Sofia kept her weight steady over the bicycle and did not tip to either side. She stayed {balanced} along the path.","question":"What does “balanced” mean here?","options":["steady without tipping","quick without stopping","quiet without speaking"],"answer":"steady without tipping","hint":"The rider does not tip to either side.","why":"“Balanced” means steady, with weight supported so something does not tip.","alt":"A young girl with brown skin checks her correctly fitted and fastened bicycle helmet beside a bicycle on a smooth traffic-free park path. An adult instructor crouches beside her to check the chin strap. A second child balances on a bicycle in the background. Closed shoes and sensible cycling safety."},{"id":"meaning-AA-29","title":"Rock-pool care","image":"assets/illustrations/rock-pools.webp","passage":"The rocks were wet and could be slippery. The children took small, careful steps and stayed {cautious} near the pools.","question":"What does “cautious” mean here?","options":["careful about possible danger","certain nothing could go wrong","eager to hurry ahead"],"answer":"careful about possible danger","hint":"The wet rocks could be slippery.","why":"“Cautious” means careful to avoid possible danger.","alt":"Two children crouch beside shallow seawater pools between flat coastal rocks at low tide. They look closely at a tiny crab and shells without touching or disturbing them. An attentive adult guide is beside them. Non-slip shoes, stable rock surfaces and gentle daylight."},{"id":"meaning-AA-30","title":"A quiet place","image":"assets/illustrations/library-friends.webp","passage":"The children settled in the reading corner, where there was little noise or interruption. The place felt {peaceful}.","question":"What does “peaceful” mean here?","options":["calm and quiet","busy and crowded","new and unfamiliar"],"answer":"calm and quiet","hint":"Look for the lack of noise and interruption.","why":"“Peaceful” means calm and quiet.","alt":"Sofia, a girl with medium-brown skin and a green cardigan, chooses a book with a colourful picture-only cover and places it on a clear library table. A friend wearing a lavender hijab reads quietly beside her. Warm low shelves, a calm reading nook and no readable lettering on spines or pages."}]}};
